{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015inN36AxPJcBmdWDfbfkX1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed worst-tier predictions for every `planned` experiment in the experiment_plan. Let me carefully go through each planned experiment and generate predictions consistent with the worst-tier definition.\n\nLet me identify all planned experiments:\n\n1. plan_010: Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2\n2. plan_011: Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\n3. plan_012: Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\n4. plan_014: Walker Walk 008e_v3 (mitigation) seeds 1-2\n\n\n5. plan_013: Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\n6. plan_020: Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\n7. plan_021: Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n8. plan_022: Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n9. plan_023: Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\n10. plan_030: RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\n11. plan_031: Actor entropy\n12. plan_032: Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\n13. plan_033: dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\n14. plan_050: Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\n15. plan_051: Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n16. plan_052: Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\n17. plan_060: Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot (Walker Walk, 1 seed)\n18. plan_040: Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\n\nThe critical failure case would be if the trained dt_emb collapse only shows up in Walker Walk and doesn't replicate across environments—that would undermine the core hypothesis about dt_embedding as a diagnostic marker for generalization.\n\nNow I'm looking at the key metrics that would define this worst-case scenario: recovery percentages in the 55-85 range, classification accuracy around 0.45-0.72, zero cross-environment mechanism replication, collapse probability staying low at 0.0-0.2, and the separating power of the diagnostic staying weak. The narrative would shift from positioning this as a universal diagnostic to framing it as a specific case study about RSSM fidelity bottlenecks.\n\nLet me work through what the worst tier predictions would look like for each experiment, starting with the Walker Walk baseline seeds where I'd expect mostly functional baselines but potentially unusual variance or one seed underperforming.\n\nThe critical failure modes I'm tracking: seed 2 of the 008e_v3 variant dropping significantly below baseline, or the untrained dt_emb showing the same nve threshold violations that should only appear in trained versions. For Cheetah and Cartpole, the trained dt_emb might fail to trigger the expected nve threshold, or worse, the untrained version triggers it too, suggesting the threshold itself is unreliable. The C6 mitigation could prove ineffective in certain environments, with imagination-based improvements bottoming out at 60-75% of baseline. The collapse probability might stay artificially low or only manifest in specific environments. And the downward trend from 009c at 148 steps by 105K iterations could replicate across more seeds, which would undermine 008f's credibility as a causal control.\n\nFor plan_010, the baseline dt=1 controls should remain stable, though one seed might exhibit slightly different value/error calibration that complicates threshold detection. For plan_011, the worst-case scenario is that seed 1 (009e) doesn't collapse at all and fails to show the nve threshold violation, dropping collapse probability to 25-33% and breaking the claim that this is a reliable diagnostic. The threshold classification itself becomes noisy, with accuracy ranging from 45-72%, meaning the 1.5x boundary no longer cleanly separates the behaviors I'm trying to distinguish.\n\nLooking at the actual data though, seed 2 (009b) already demonstrated nve>1.5x consistently, so even if seed 1 fails to show it, I'd still have 2 out of 3 seeds exceeding the threshold. The worst-case would make 009e the anomalous outlier that doesn't sustain nve above 1.5x at later checkpoints. For plan_012, I'm now checking whether untrained dt_emb seeds might also cross the 1.5x threshold under worst conditions, which would blur the distinction I'm trying to establish between trained and untrained embeddings.\n\nLooking at the Cheetah Run results, I need to see whether the cross-environment mechanism replication holds up under worst-case scenarios.\n\nThe core risk is that the dt_embedding mechanism might be Walker-specific—if the trained embedding doesn't trigger the high nve behavior in Cheetah, or if even untrained embeddings show similar nve values, then the whole story breaks. Same concern applies to Cartpole Swingup. Beyond that, I'm checking whether the RSSM fidelity gap explanation holds across environments, and whether the supporting analyses—actor entropy, value distributions, and dt embedding similarity—actually show clear patterns or just noise.\n\nNow I need to pin down specific metric values and thresholds for each experiment's expected results, starting with clarifying the seed lineage for plan_011 and what the actual nve peaks look like under the worst-case scenario. Looking at the experiment statuses, I need to focus on the planned experiments: plan_010, plan_011, plan_012, and plan_014 are all marked as planned, while plan_013 appears incomplete. For each of these, I should examine the detailed data for the experiments that are still queued or haven't started yet. Now I'm reviewing the experimental results across the different seed configurations. Plan 009a is already running and converging well around 919, so that baseline is solid. For the worst-case scenarios, the baseline seeds should hold up fine with dt=1, though the v/e calibration at 35K might shift the optimal threshold by around 15%. Looking at plan 011 with the 008d seeds, I can see that 009b already peaked at 2.05x early on but self-corrected down to 1.62x by 45K without collapsing, and the additional seeds under worst-case conditions stay consistently below 1.5x with peaks around 1.3x, so across all three seeds there's no collapse pattern emerging.\n\nWait, I need to clarify the configuration details here—008d ran at H=8 and seed 0 collapsed at that setting, and 009b was also the 008d config at seed 2 with the same H=8 architecture. 009e replicates that same 008d configuration with subsample enabled and trained dt_emb. Under worst-case conditions, 009e shows an nve peak around 1.35x at 35K and beyond without exceeding 1.5x, which means the collapse pattern doesn't replicate even under stress.\n\nLooking at the collapse probability for trained dt_emb, I'm getting 1 out of 3 seeds collapsing (33%), but the worst tier specifies a range of 0.0 to 0.2, so this doesn't quite fit unless I'm reassessing 008d seed 0's collapse or 009e also fails to sustain performance. The worst tier bounds are meant for the final assessment across all environments, so maybe the picture changes once I factor in results from Cheetah and Cartpole.\n\nNow I'm ready to write out the specific predictions. I'll keep them grounded in the worst-tier narrative without getting too caught up in exact probability ranges. For the baselines in plan_010, I'm expecting eval scores around 900-940 with stable value-to-eval ratios in the 65-72% range. For plan_011, I need to account for 009b already showing no collapse with transient nve spikes, and then assess what happens with 009e under the worst-case scenario.\n\nThe key differentiator is whether nve peaks exceed that 1.5x threshold. If 009e stays below it at around 1.35x, the separating power drops slightly but the claim holds. However, for plan_012 with 009f, if nve actually crosses 1.5x at 95K, that breaks the entire \"untrained never exceeds 1.5x\" classification. For plan_014, I need to clarify the seed 1 situation with 008e_v3 since it apparently used the same data as seed 0.\n\nLooking at the registry more carefully, seed 1 shows an identical eval trajectory to the original run, which suggests either it's a duplicate entry or seed 1 hasn't actually been executed separately yet. I need to determine whether the existing data is truly seed 1 or if I'm looking at seed 0 recorded twice.\n\nFor the Cheetah Run experiments, the cross-environment mechanism replication factor is zero under worst-case conditions, meaning the baseline performance holds around 700-800 eval returns, but the trained dt_emb variant doesn't trigger the delusional critic pattern like it does in Walker—instead showing only mild degradation to 55-65% of baseline, while the untrained variant exhibits a smaller nve multiplier around 1.3-1.5x that blurs the distinction between conditions.\n\nThe same replication failure appears in Cartpole across plans 050-052. For the RSSM fidelity analysis, the gap patterns are inconsistent across environments, with Cheetah potentially showing smaller observation gaps at dt=2 compared to Walker, and reward gaps that don't correlate cleanly with collapse. Actor entropy under worst-case doesn't clearly separate healthy from collapsed configs—collapsed setups show entropy decreasing as the policy converges to the wrong behavior rather than increasing, which weakens the narrative. Value distribution overlap between V(s) and Monte Carlo returns remains substantial even in collapsed configs early on, making it difficult to distinguish from noise. The dt_embedding cosine similarity metric shows high values around...\n\nWriting YAML configuration... I'm noticing that the embedding-based predictions are unreliable, so I'll compile everything into a structured format instead. Looking at the plan_008 registry, I see that exp_008e_v3 has some completed seeds with identical performance numbers across different runs, which suggests potential data duplication—if seed 1 is actually a copy of seed 0, the real results under worst-case conditions would be considerably lower, and the same applies to seed 2 which is still running.\n\nNow I'm organizing this comprehensively by plan ID with inline metric tables and brief plot descriptions.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":308,"cache_read_input_tokens":42241,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":308},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0c2338d-48fd-4569-bbff-a85af5e5ab47","uuid":"69fc421e-a26a-4743-b26b-199f155fd118"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015inN36AxPJcBmdWDfbfkX1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心reframe：从\"诊断temporal abstraction的通用失败机制\"转向\"DreamerV3 RSSM fidelity\n  作为temporal abstraction的瓶颈——一个受控案例研究\"。主贡献从diagnostic finding变为\n  diagnostic methodology（factorial ablation框架 + nve监控协议）。将non-replication\n  本身作为finding——\"temporal abstraction的失败模式是architecture×environment交互的产物，\n  不存在universal failure mode\"。C6降级为environment-conditional guideline。\n  标题候选：\"When Does Temporal Abstraction Break World Models? An Empirical\n  Investigation of DreamerV3\"。CoRL审稿预期：borderline。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"2 additional seeds for baseline v/e calibration\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_009d_eval_return_105K: 908\n      seed1_009d_eval_return_last10_mean: 935\n      seed1_009d_ve_ratio_35K: 0.215\n      seed1_009d_ve_ratio_45K: 0.305\n      seed1_009d_ve_ratio_105K: 0.635\n      seed1_009d_ve_stable: \"67-71% from 135K+\"\n      seed2_009a_eval_return_105K: 919\n      seed2_009a_eval_return_last10_mean: 942\n      seed2_009a_ve_ratio_35K: 0.248\n      seed2_009a_ve_ratio_105K: 0.699\n      seed2_009a_ve_stable: \"69-71% from 245K+\"\n      IQM_baseline_3seeds_105K: 916\n      cross_seed_std_eval_105K: 12.3\n      cross_seed_ve_35K_range: \"[0.215, 0.248]\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Baseline (dt=1) 本身不受 worst 档影响——它是标准 DreamerV3 在 Walker Walk 的收敛行为，\n      三个 seed 均应收敛到 900-960 范围。但 worst 档的隐患在于 v/e 校准的 seed 间变异：\n      seed 1 的 ve_ratio@35K 可能偏低至 0.215（vs seed 0 的 0.241），这意味着以 seed 0\n      校准的 1.5x 阈值（即绝对 v/e=0.362）在 seed 1 的背景下实际对应 1.68x normalized，\n      引入 ~12% 的阈值偏移。这不影响 baseline 本身的结论，但会在后续 nve 计算中放大噪声，\n      为 cross-seed 的 threshold 可靠性埋下问题。seed 2 (009a) 已确认收敛正常。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Walker Baseline Cross-Seed Summary\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"ve@35K\", \"ve@105K\", \"ve_stable\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"seed 0 (001)\", 916, 0.241, 0.656, \"69-72%\"]\n          - [\"seed 1 (009d)\", 908, 0.215, 0.635, \"67-71%\"]\n          - [\"seed 2 (009a)\", 919, 0.248, 0.699, \"69-71%\"]\n          - [\"IQM ± CI\", \"916 ± 14\", \"0.235 ± 0.017\", \"0.663 ± 0.033\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三 seed baseline 学习曲线叠加图，eval return vs step，显示紧密收敛 band\"\n      - \"三 seed v/e ratio vs step，标注 35K 处各 seed 的校准值差异\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 本身稳健，但 v/e@35K 的 15% cross-seed 变异意味着 nve=1.5x 阈值在\n      不同 seed 组合下对应不同的绝对 v/e 水平。在 worst 档中这个变异被放大——当 Cheetah/Cartpole\n      的 baseline v/e 校准可能与 Walker 差异更大时，统一阈值的 cross-env 可靠性进一步下降。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"Replicate delusional critic collapse with 2 more seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed2_009b_status: \"DONE — no collapse, transient nve>1.5x\"\n      seed2_009b_eval_105K: 268\n      seed2_009b_nve_peak: 2.05\n      seed2_009b_nve_peak_step: \"25K (early, before baseline v/e converges)\"\n      seed2_009b_nve_45K: 1.62\n      seed2_009b_nve_105K: 0.38\n      seed2_009b_collapse: false\n      seed1_009e_eval_25K: 155\n      seed1_009e_eval_35K: 178\n      seed1_009e_eval_45K: 192\n      seed1_009e_eval_55K: 175\n      seed1_009e_eval_105K: 215\n      seed1_009e_nve_25K: 1.45\n      seed1_009e_nve_35K: 1.35\n      seed1_009e_nve_45K: 1.28\n      seed1_009e_nve_55K: 1.15\n      seed1_009e_nve_105K: 0.82\n      seed1_009e_collapse: false\n      collapse_count_of_3: \"1/3 (33%)\"\n      nve_above_1_5x_at_35Kplus: \"2/3 (008d seed 0, 009b seed 2)\"\n      nve_threshold_classification_accuracy: 0.67\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档核心预测：009e (seed 1) 的 nve 在 35K+ 始终不超过 1.5x。机制：trained dt_emb\n      的 delusional critic 效应依赖 RSSM 在 dt=2 时的预测偏差方向——如果 seed 1 的初始化\n      恰好让 RSSM 在 dt=2 时产生偏保守（而非偏乐观）的 reward 预测，trained dt_emb 的\n      conditioning 反而会让 value function 低估（不是高估）dt=2 trajectory 的价值。\n      009e 的 nve@25K=1.45x（接近但未达 1.5x），然后随训练进行单调下降至 0.82x@105K。\n      这意味着 1.5x 阈值在 trained dt_emb 组的分类能力降至 2/3（不再是 2/2），总体\n      classification accuracy 从 4/4=100% 降至 4/6=67%。009b@25K 的 2.05x 本身是\n      early false positive（baseline v/e 仅 0.087 时比率不稳定），在 35K+ 仅有\n      45K 的 1.62x 真正可靠。collapse 概率仅 1/3=33%，且唯一的 collapse（008d seed 0）\n      仅在 H=8 配置下观察到。如果 009e 也是 H=8 配置但不 collapse，进一步说明\n      collapse 是高度随机的罕见事件，而非 trained dt_emb 的确定性后果。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008d Config Cross-Seed nve Trajectory\"\n        columns: [\"step\", \"seed 0 (008d) nve\", \"seed 1 (009e) nve\", \"seed 2 (009b) nve\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"25K\", \"1.78*\", \"1.45*\", \"2.05*\"]\n          - [\"35K\", \"1.71\", \"1.35\", \"1.24\"]\n          - [\"45K\", \"2.09\", \"1.28\", \"1.62\"]\n          - [\"55K\", \"4.12 → collapse\", \"1.15\", \"1.41\"]\n          - [\"105K\", \"collapsed\", \"0.82\", \"0.38\"]\n        note: \"*25K values unreliable due to low baseline v/e (0.087)\"\n      - name: \"1.5x Threshold Classification (Updated)\"\n        columns: [\"group\", \"seed\", \"nve>1.5x at 35K+?\", \"collapse?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", \"008d s0\", \"YES (sustained)\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", \"009e s1\", \"NO (peak 1.35)\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", \"009b s2\", \"YES (transient)\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"no dt_emb\", \"008f s0\", \"NO (peak 1.02)\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"no dt_emb\", \"009f s1\", \"YES (1.52x@95K)\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"no dt_emb\", \"009c s2\", \"NO (peak 1.26)\", \"NO\"]\n        note: \"Classification accuracy drops to 4/6 = 67%\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三 seed nve 轨迹叠加图，1.5x 阈值线标注，显示 seed 1 始终在阈值下方\"\n      - \"eval return 三 seed 叠加，仅 seed 0 展示 collapse pattern\"\n    analysis: >\n      009e 不超过 1.5x 阈值直接削弱 C2 的 \"reliable diagnostic marker\" 定位。\n      nve>1.5x 不再是 trained dt_emb 的确定性后果，而是概率性后果（~67% 的 seed 会触发）。\n      更关键的是 collapse 概率仅 1/3——即使 nve 超过 1.5x（如 009b），系统也能\n      自我纠正。论文中必须承认 \"nve>1.5x is a risk indicator, not a deterministic\n      predictor\"，这显著削弱了诊断价值的叙事。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control stability with 2 more seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed2_009c_status: \"DONE — decline to 148@105K, nve=1.14x\"\n      seed2_009c_eval_105K: 148\n      seed2_009c_nve_105K: 1.14\n      seed2_009c_trend: \"decline after 75K peak\"\n      seed1_009f_eval_25K: 175\n      seed1_009f_eval_35K: 195\n      seed1_009f_eval_45K: 210\n      seed1_009f_eval_55K: 188\n      seed1_009f_eval_65K: 230\n      seed1_009f_eval_75K: 265\n      seed1_009f_eval_85K: 285\n      seed1_009f_eval_95K: 310\n      seed1_009f_eval_105K: 275\n      seed1_009f_nve_35K: 0.85\n      seed1_009f_nve_45K: 0.92\n      seed1_009f_nve_55K: 1.08\n      seed1_009f_nve_65K: 1.22\n      seed1_009f_nve_75K: 1.38\n      seed1_009f_nve_85K: 1.45\n      seed1_009f_nve_95K: 1.52\n      seed1_009f_nve_105K: 1.35\n      seed1_009f_nve_crosses_1_5x: true\n      untrained_group_nve_above_1_5x: \"1/3 seeds (009f)\"\n      causal_control_reliability: \"compromised\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档核心问题之一：009c 已确认 008f 的保护不 robust（decline to 148，nve=1.14x\n      且上升趋势）。009f 在 worst 档下进一步恶化——nve 在 95K 触及 1.52x（超过 1.5x 阈值），\n      尽管随后回落至 1.35x。机制：dt_embed_dim=0 去掉了 dt conditioning，但 RSSM 仍然\n      隐式学习了 dt=1/dt=2 的状态转移差异（通过观察到的 state transition 模式）。在某些\n      seed 中，这种隐式学习足以让 value function 逐渐开发出对 dt>1 trajectory 的偏好，\n      只是速度比 trained dt_emb 慢得多（008f s1@95K 才达到 1.52x vs 008d s0@35K 就达到\n      1.71x）。这意味着 dt_embedding 是 amplifier 但不是 sole enabler——RSSM 本身在\n      长时间训练后也能产生类似（但更弱的）效应。这直接削弱了 \"dt_embedding is the\n      necessary and sufficient cause\" 的因果声明。009c 的 decline pattern 与 009f 的\n      borderline nve 共同表明 008f 不是可靠的 causal control——\"eliminates\" 和\n      \"significantly delays\" 都过强，实际效果是 \"partially attenuates with high\n      seed-dependent variance\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008f Config Cross-Seed Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"metric\", \"seed 0 (008f)\", \"seed 1 (009f)\", \"seed 2 (009c)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"eval@105K\", 503, 275, 148]\n          - [\"nve peak (35K+)\", \"0.97x@55K\", \"1.52x@95K\", \"1.14x@105K\"]\n          - [\"nve@105K\", \"0.30x\", \"1.35x\", \"1.14x\"]\n          - [\"trend\", \"zigzag recovery\", \"slow rise then mild decline\", \"peak-then-decline\"]\n          - [\"nve>1.5x?\", \"NO\", \"YES (transient)\", \"NO\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"008f 三 seed eval + nve 叠加图，显示极高 cross-seed variance（503 vs 275 vs 148）\"\n      - \"与 008d 三 seed 对比：nve 分布 overlap 区域标注\"\n    analysis: >\n      008f 三 seed 的 eval@105K 范围为 148-503（3.4x 差异），cross-seed variance 极大，\n      使其作为 causal control 不可靠。更严重的是 009f 的 nve 突破 1.5x，意味着\n      untrained/no-dt-emb 组也存在 nve>1.5x 的 seed——阈值的 separating power 从 4/4\n      降至 4/6 (67%)，不再具有 \"perfect classification\" 的论文叙事价值。C2 的因果声明\n      必须软化为 \"trained dt_emb significantly increases the probability and speed\n      of pathological overestimation, but does not exclusively cause it\"。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 (mitigation) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"Multi-seed validation of dt=1 imagination mitigation\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 870\n      seed0_nve_105K: 0.80\n      seed1_eval_25K: 142\n      seed1_eval_35K: 225\n      seed1_eval_45K: 310\n      seed1_eval_55K: 380\n      seed1_eval_65K: 425\n      seed1_eval_75K: 460\n      seed1_eval_85K: 495\n      seed1_eval_95K: 540\n      seed1_eval_105K: 590\n      seed1_nve_35K: 0.98\n      seed1_nve_45K: 0.95\n      seed1_nve_55K: 0.92\n      seed1_nve_65K: 0.85\n      seed1_nve_75K: 0.82\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.88\n      seed1_vs_baseline_105K: \"-35.6%\"\n      seed2_eval_25K: 135\n      seed2_eval_35K: 210\n      seed2_eval_45K: 285\n      seed2_eval_55K: 350\n      seed2_eval_65K: 390\n      seed2_eval_75K: 440\n      seed2_eval_85K: 480\n      seed2_eval_95K: 510\n      seed2_eval_105K: 550\n      seed2_nve_35K: 1.02\n      seed2_nve_45K: 0.96\n      seed2_nve_55K: 0.90\n      seed2_nve_65K: 0.88\n      seed2_nve_75K: 0.85\n      seed2_nve_105K: 0.91\n      seed2_vs_baseline_105K: \"-40.0%\"\n      IQM_3seeds_eval_105K: 670\n      IQM_3seeds_pct_baseline: 73\n      cross_seed_std: 173\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档核心假设：C6 的 95% baseline recovery 是 seed-specific 的幸运结果。\n      seed 0 的 870 可能是因为其初始化恰好让 RSSM 在 dt=1 imagination 下产生了与\n      pure baseline 接近的训练信号分布。seed 1 和 seed 2 可能面临不同的问题：\n      subsample ON 意味着训练数据包含 dt=2 transitions，这些 transition 的 RSSM 表征\n      即使在 dt=1 imagination 时也会 \"污染\" latent state 的学习。在某些 seed 中，\n      这种污染效应更明显——RSSM 对 dt=2 transition 分配了更多 representational capacity，\n      导致 dt=1 imagination 的 rollout quality 反而下降。结果是 seed 1 仅达 590\n      (64% baseline)，seed 2 仅达 550 (60% baseline)。IQM 约 670 (73% baseline)，\n      远低于 seed 0 的 95%。nve 保持健康（0.85-1.02x），但 performance 本身不够。\n      在 worst 档下，C6 从 \"practical zero-cost mitigation (95% recovery)\" 降级为\n      \"environment-conditional partial mitigation (58-95% recovery, high variance)\"，\n      显著削弱 actionable takeaway 的说服力。论文中 008e_v3 不能作为推荐方案呈现，\n      只能作为 \"one possible direction\" 附带 high-variance caveat。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008e_v3 Mitigation Cross-Seed Results\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"% baseline\", \"nve@105K\", \"collapse?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"seed 0\", 870, \"95%\", \"0.80x\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"seed 1\", 590, \"64%\", \"0.88x\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"seed 2\", 550, \"60%\", \"0.91x\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"IQM ± CI\", \"670 ± 185\", \"73% ± 20%\", \"0.86x ± 0.06\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"008e_v3 三 seed 学习曲线叠加，seed 0 远高于 seed 1/2，显示 recovery 的 seed-dependence\"\n      - \"与 baseline 三 seed 对比的 IQM bar chart，error bar 显示巨大 CI\"\n    analysis: >\n      C6 recovery 的 IQM 73% 落入 worst 档指标范围 [58,82]。20pp CI 使得\n      \"practical mitigation\" 的叙事站不住——审稿人会质疑 \"a mitigation that recovers\n      60-95% depending on seed is not actionable\"。必须 reframe 为 conditional\n      guideline，强调 dt=1 imagination 至少避免 collapse（三 seed 无一 collapse，\n      nve 均健康），即使 performance recovery 不一致。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression with 2 more seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_55K: 420\n      seed1_eval_65K: 380\n      seed1_eval_75K: 350\n      seed1_eval_85K: 390\n      seed1_eval_95K: 410\n      seed1_eval_105K: 450\n      seed1_nve_55K: 0.85\n      seed1_nve_65K: 0.72\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.68\n      seed1_pattern: \"single weak V-recovery, lower amplitude than seed 0\"\n      seed2_eval_55K: 350\n      seed2_eval_65K: 310\n      seed2_eval_75K: 340\n      seed2_eval_85K: 360\n      seed2_eval_95K: 330\n      seed2_eval_105K: 380\n      seed2_nve_55K: 0.88\n      seed2_nve_65K: 0.78\n      seed2_nve_105K: 0.75\n      seed2_pattern: \"oscillating plateau, no clear V-recovery\"\n      IQM_3seeds_105K: 536\n      IQM_pct_baseline: \"59%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      seed 0 的 778@105K (85% baseline) 和 double V-recovery pattern 在 worst 档下\n      不被 replicate。原因：untrained dt_emb 的保护依赖于 random embedding 恰好不与\n      RSSM 的 dt=2 状态表征 align——如果 random initialization 碰巧与某个有意义的\n      dt-相关方向 partially aligned，保护效果减弱。seed 1 展示弱化版 V-recovery\n      （amplitude 更小，peak 仅 450 vs seed 0 的 778），seed 2 则表现为无方向性的\n      oscillating plateau（330-380 范围）。nve 仍保持在 baseline 以下（0.68-0.88x），\n      确认 value growth suppression 的方向性成立，但 performance recovery 的幅度\n      高度 seed-dependent。C3 的 \"substantive protection\" 声明在 IQM 仅 59% baseline\n      的情况下需要大幅软化。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008a Untrained dt_emb Cross-Seed Summary\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"% baseline\", \"nve@105K\", \"pattern\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"seed 0\", 778, \"85%\", \"0.59x\", \"double V-recovery\"]\n          - [\"seed 1\", 450, \"49%\", \"0.68x\", \"weak single V-recovery\"]\n          - [\"seed 2\", 380, \"41%\", \"0.75x\", \"oscillating plateau\"]\n          - [\"IQM\", 536, \"59%\", \"0.67x\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三 seed eval 轨迹叠加，seed 0 的 V-recovery pattern 在其他 seed 中不复现\"\n    analysis: >\n      nve suppression 方向一致（三 seed 均 <1.0x），但 performance recovery 差异巨大。\n      C3 需要 rewrite：\"untrained dt_emb reliably suppresses value growth below baseline\n      levels, but performance recovery is highly variable (41-85% baseline)\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in second DMC environment\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 720\n      seed1_eval_105K: 695\n      seed2_eval_105K: 740\n      IQM_3seeds: 718\n      seed0_ve_35K: 0.185\n      seed0_ve_105K: 0.58\n      seed1_ve_35K: 0.170\n      seed2_ve_35K: 0.195\n      ve_stable_range: \"55-62% from 135K+\"\n      convergence_step: \"~85K (faster than Walker's ~135K)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah Run baseline 应正常收敛——DreamerV3 在此环境有良好 track record。但\n      v/e 校准值与 Walker 显著不同：Cheetah 的 ve@35K 约 0.18（vs Walker 的 0.24），\n      ve 收敛更快（~85K vs ~135K），stable range 更低（55-62% vs 69-72%）。这种\n      环境间的 v/e 校准差异意味着 Walker 中 calibrated 的 1.5x nve 阈值在 Cheetah\n      中对应不同的绝对 v/e 水平（0.18×1.5=0.27 vs Walker 的 0.24×1.5=0.36），\n      使 cross-env 阈值统一变得更复杂。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah Run Baseline\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"ve@35K\", \"ve@105K\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"seed 0\", 720, 0.185, 0.58]\n          - [\"seed 1\", 695, 0.170, 0.56]\n          - [\"seed 2\", 740, 0.195, 0.61]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah baseline 三 seed 学习曲线，与 Walker baseline 对比标注收敛速度差异\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 正常但 v/e 校准差异为后续 cross-env nve 比较制造了 confound。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: \"Replicate delusional critic collapse in Cheetah Run\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_35K: 385\n      seed0_eval_45K: 410\n      seed0_eval_55K: 395\n      seed0_eval_65K: 380\n      seed0_eval_105K: 420\n      seed0_nve_35K: 1.15\n      seed0_nve_45K: 1.22\n      seed0_nve_55K: 1.18\n      seed0_nve_105K: 0.95\n      seed0_collapse: false\n      seed1_eval_105K: 380\n      seed1_nve_peak: 1.30\n      seed1_nve_105K: 1.05\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 350\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.25\n      seed2_nve_105K: 1.10\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      IQM_3seeds_105K: 383\n      IQM_pct_baseline: \"53%\"\n      nve_above_1_5x_count: \"0/3\"\n      collapse_count: \"0/3\"\n      cross_env_mechanism_replication: 0\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档核心预测：Cheetah Run 中 trained dt_emb 不触发 nve>1.5x。原因：\n      Cheetah Run 的 RSSM 在 dt=2 的预测质量比 Walker Walk 更好——Cheetah 的\n      dynamics 更平滑（近似线性 forward motion），RSSM 的 dt=2 预测误差更小（预计\n      obs_gap ~1.4x vs Walker 的 2.04x）。更低的 RSSM fidelity gap 意味着 trained\n      dt_emb 的 conditioning 虽然精确，但它 condition 的目标（dt=2 predictions）\n      与真实 dynamics 的偏差更小——value function 的 overestimation 被限制在 1.1-1.3x\n      范围，不足以触发正反馈 loop。performance 仍然 degraded（53% baseline），但\n      degradation 模式是 \"slow plateau\" 而非 \"delusional critic collapse\"。\n      这直接证明 Walker 中观察到的 nve>1.5x → collapse 机制是 environment-specific\n      的：它依赖于 RSSM 在特定环境的 dt=2 预测误差大小，而非 trained dt_emb 的\n      universal 效应。三个 seed 无一超过 1.5x，cross_env_mechanism_replication = 0。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah Trained dt_emb Results\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"% baseline\", \"nve peak (35K+)\", \"nve@105K\", \"collapse\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"seed 0\", 420, \"58%\", \"1.22x@45K\", \"0.95x\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"seed 1\", 380, \"53%\", \"1.30x@55K\", \"1.05x\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"seed 2\", 350, \"49%\", \"1.25x@45K\", \"1.10x\", \"NO\"]\n      - name: \"Cross-Environment nve>1.5x Summary\"\n        columns: [\"environment\", \"trained dt_emb seeds exceeding 1.5x\", \"collapse seeds\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"2/3 (67%)\", \"1/3 (33%)\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah vs Walker nve 轨迹对比图：Walker 展示 >1.5x 发散，Cheetah 稳定在 1.0-1.3x\"\n      - \"Cheetah eval 学习曲线（三 seed），无 collapse pattern，仅 plateau degradation\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 的 non-replication 是 worst 档最具杀伤力的发现。它证明 \"trained dt_emb\n      → nve>1.5x → collapse\" 不是 universal mechanism，而是 environment-conditional。\n      论文叙事必须 reframe：delusional critic 的触发条件是 \"sufficient RSSM fidelity\n      gap at dt>1\"，这在不同环境中可能满足也可能不满足。C2 从 \"trained dt_emb\n      reliably triggers pathological overestimation\" 变为 \"trained dt_emb amplifies\n      RSSM fidelity gap into overestimation, with magnitude depending on\n      environment-specific prediction difficulty at dt>1\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control in Cheetah Run\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 390\n      seed0_nve_105K: 0.88\n      seed1_eval_105K: 370\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.95\n      seed2_eval_105K: 355\n      seed2_nve_105K: 1.02\n      IQM_3seeds_105K: 372\n      IQM_pct_baseline: \"52%\"\n      nve_above_1_5x_count: \"0/3\"\n      trained_vs_untrained_eval_gap: \"~3% (383 vs 372)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah 中 trained dt_emb (plan_021) 和 no-dt_emb (plan_022) 的 performance\n      差异极小（383 vs 372，~3%），远小于 Walker 中的差异（008d collapse vs 008f 503）。\n      原因：Cheetah 中 RSSM fidelity gap 本身就小，所以 dt_emb 的有无对结果影响不大——\n      degradation 主要来自 subsample ON 导致的学习信号减少和 shorter effective horizon，\n      而非 delusional critic。nve 保持在 0.88-1.02x 范围，与 plan_021 的 0.95-1.10x\n      高度重叠。这意味着在 Cheetah 中，dt_emb 作为因果变量几乎无 separating power——\n      trained vs untrained 的 nve 分布 overlap 严重。C2 的因果论证在 Cheetah 中\n      完全不成立。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah: Trained vs No dt_emb Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"config\", \"IQM eval@105K\", \"IQM nve@105K\", \"gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"trained dt_emb (021)\", 383, \"1.03x\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"no dt_emb (022)\", 372, \"0.95x\", \"~3% eval, 0.08x nve\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah trained vs untrained dt_emb 的 nve 分布 violin plot，显示完全 overlap\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 中 dt_emb 因果效应接近零。degradation 是 uniform 的，不区分 trained/untrained。\n      这进一步支持 \"Walker-specific mechanism\" 结论。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression in Cheetah Run\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 520\n      seed1_eval_105K: 490\n      seed2_eval_105K: 540\n      IQM_3seeds_105K: 517\n      IQM_pct_baseline: \"72%\"\n      seed0_nve_105K: 0.78\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.85\n      seed2_nve_105K: 0.72\n      v_recovery_pattern: \"gradual improvement, no distinct V-shape\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      subsample OFF 在 Cheetah 中带来更多训练数据，performance 提升至 72% baseline\n      （vs subsample ON 的 52-53%）。但 Cheetah 中没有 delusional critic 问题（因 RSSM\n      fidelity gap 小），所以 untrained dt_emb 的 \"value suppression\" 效应无从体现——\n      nve 在 0.72-0.85x 范围，但 trained dt_emb 组也在 0.95-1.10x（无 pathological），\n      两组的 nve 差异远小于 Walker（Walker 中 untrained 0.59-0.93x vs trained 1.71-4.12x，\n      差异巨大；Cheetah 中 untrained 0.72-0.85x vs trained 0.95-1.10x，差异仅 0.2x）。\n      C3 的 \"preventing optimistic drift\" 在 Cheetah 中不具意义——因为 trained dt_emb\n      本身就不产生 optimistic drift。学习曲线呈现渐进上升而非 Walker 的 V-recovery，\n      进一步说明 Walker 的 zigzag pattern 是 environment-specific 的 transient dynamics。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah Untrained dt_emb (no subsample)\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"% baseline\", \"nve@105K\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"seed 0\", 520, \"72%\", \"0.78x\"]\n          - [\"seed 1\", 490, \"68%\", \"0.85x\"]\n          - [\"seed 2\", 540, \"75%\", \"0.72x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah 四配置（baseline, trained, no-dt-emb, untrained-no-subsample）IQM bar chart\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 中 subsample ON/OFF 的效应（52% vs 72%）大于 dt_emb trained/untrained\n      的效应（~3%），说明在此环境中 primary degradation factor 是 learning signal\n      reduction，不是 delusional critic。与 Walker 的因果结构完全不同。\n\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: \"Quantify RSSM fidelity gap across models\"\n    expected_results:\n      cheetah_baseline_obs_gap: 1.35\n      cheetah_baseline_reward_gap: 1.18\n      cheetah_008d_obs_gap: 1.25\n      cheetah_008d_reward_gap: 1.85\n      cheetah_008f_obs_gap: 1.40\n      cheetah_008f_reward_gap: 1.02\n      walker_vs_cheetah_obs_gap_ratio: \"2.04x / 1.35x = Walker fidelity gap 51% larger\"\n      cartpole_baseline_obs_gap: 1.20\n      cross_env_fidelity_gap_correlation_with_collapse: \"weak (r ≈ 0.45)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 RSSM fidelity 分析揭示一个尴尬事实：Walker 的 obs_gap (2.04x) 远高于\n      Cheetah (1.35x) 和 Cartpole (1.20x)。这解释了为什么 delusional critic 仅在\n      Walker 中触发——RSSM 在 Walker 的 dt=2 步预测质量显著更差。但这也意味着 \"RSSM\n      fidelity gap → delusional critic\" 的因果链虽然在方向上成立（gap 大 → 更容易\n      overestimate），但 gap 的大小是 environment-specific 的，无法预先判断哪个环境会\n      触发。Cheetah 中 trained dt_emb 的 reward_gap (1.85x) 虽然高于 baseline (1.18x)，\n      但远低于 Walker 008d 的 2.78x——不足以驱动正反馈 loop。fidelity gap 与 collapse\n      的相关性较弱（r≈0.45），因为中间变量太多（seed 随机性、training dynamics、\n      environment reward structure）。RSSM fidelity table 升级为核心贡献的叙事方向\n      在 worst 档下是对的，但贡献从 \"predictive tool\" 降级为 \"post-hoc explanatory\n      framework\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-Environment RSSM Fidelity Gap\"\n        columns: [\"environment\", \"config\", \"obs_gap (dt2/dt1)\", \"reward_gap\", \"collapse?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker\", \"baseline\", \"2.04x\", \"1.56x\", \"N/A\"]\n          - [\"Walker\", \"trained dt_emb\", \"1.30x*\", \"2.78x\", \"1/3 seeds\"]\n          - [\"Walker\", \"no dt_emb\", \"2.75x\", \"1.01x\", \"0/3 seeds\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", \"baseline\", \"1.35x\", \"1.18x\", \"N/A\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", \"trained dt_emb\", \"1.25x\", \"1.85x\", \"0/3 seeds\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", \"no dt_emb\", \"1.40x\", \"1.02x\", \"0/3 seeds\"]\n        note: \"*Walker 008d obs_gap 低因模型已整体崩塌（dt=1 绝对误差 3x baseline）\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-env RSSM fidelity gap scatter plot: obs_gap vs nve_peak，标注 Walker vs Cheetah 的分离\"\n    analysis: >\n      Fidelity gap 解释了 cross-env 差异但不预测它。论文中 RSSM fidelity table 作为\n      \"post-hoc diagnostic\"，价值有限——审稿人会问 \"how do I know a priori if my\n      environment has sufficient fidelity gap to worry about delusional critic?\"\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: \"Plot actor entropy for healthy vs collapsed configs\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_s0_entropy_35K: 3.2\n      walker_008d_s0_entropy_45K: 2.8\n      walker_008d_s0_entropy_55K: 2.1\n      walker_008d_s0_pattern: \"monotonic decrease even during collapse\"\n      walker_008a_s0_entropy_55K: 3.5\n      walker_008a_s0_entropy_105K: 3.1\n      walker_baseline_entropy_55K: 3.8\n      walker_baseline_entropy_105K: 3.0\n      entropy_separation: \"weak — collapsed config shows lower entropy but overlaps with late-training baseline\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 actor entropy 分析不产生 clean separation。预期 collapsed 配置（008d）\n      的 entropy 在 collapse 前单调下降——这看起来像是 policy 过度确信而非困惑，但\n      baseline 在晚期训练中也展示 entropy 下降（3.8→3.0），使得区分变得模糊。\n      008d 的 entropy 在 55K (collapse 时) 约 2.1，而 baseline@55K 约 3.8（差异明显），\n      但 008d@35K=3.2 与 baseline@95K=3.2 完全重合——如果不知道 step 信息，无法仅凭\n      entropy 值判断是否即将 collapse。entropy 不是一个可用的 early warning signal，\n      削弱了将其作为 diagnostic metric 的价值。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Actor Entropy Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"config\", \"step\", \"actor_entropy\", \"eval_return\", \"status\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"008d s0\", \"35K\", 3.2, 146, \"pre-collapse\"]\n          - [\"008d s0\", \"55K\", 2.1, 83, \"collapsed\"]\n          - [\"baseline\", \"35K\", 4.1, 389, \"healthy\"]\n          - [\"baseline\", \"55K\", 3.8, 626, \"healthy\"]\n          - [\"baseline\", \"95K\", 3.2, 920, \"converged\"]\n          - [\"008a s0\", \"55K\", 3.5, 488, \"V-recovery dip\"]\n          - [\"008a s0\", \"105K\", 3.1, 778, \"recovering\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Actor entropy vs step 多配置叠加图，collapsed 和 late-stage healthy 有 overlap region\"\n    analysis: >\n      Actor entropy 作为 standalone diagnostic 不具备足够 separating power。可作为\n      nve 的 supplementary metric，但不增加独立的 diagnostic 价值。对论文贡献边际。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: \"Distribution plots of V(s) vs Monte Carlo return\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_35K_value_mean: 60.2\n      walker_008d_35K_mc_return_mean: 146\n      walker_008d_35K_value_spread: \"bimodal: cluster near 0 + long right tail to 200\"\n      walker_008d_45K_value_shift: \"right tail extends to 350, MC returns peaked at 141\"\n      walker_baseline_35K_overlap: \"high — values well-calibrated, V(s) ≈ 0.8-1.2x MC\"\n      walker_008a_35K_overlap: \"moderate — V(s) slightly below MC (0.6-0.9x)\"\n      cross_env_consistency: \"Cheetah shows minimal V(s) divergence even for trained dt_emb\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 value distribution 分析在 Walker 中展示预期的 trained dt_emb 偏差——\n      008d 的 V(s) 分布出现右偏 heavy tail，高估部分 state 的 value。但问题在于：\n      (1) @35K 时这种 right tail 可能仍在 \"正常探索\" 范围内，和 baseline 的 V(s)\n      分布 overlap 显著；(2) 只有到 45K+ 才能清晰看到 divergence，此时 nve 已经\n      标记了问题——value distribution 分析没有提供比 nve 更早的 warning；(3) 在\n      Cheetah 中，trained dt_emb 的 V(s) 分布与 baseline 高度重叠（因为 nve 仅\n      1.1-1.3x），使得这个分析在 cross-env 上不一致。worst 档下这个分析是 \"confirms\n      nve findings with more detail but no additional predictive power\"。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"V(s) vs MC return scatter plot at 35K/45K/55K for 008d vs baseline\"\n      - \"V(s) distribution histogram overlay: 008d right-skewed vs baseline symmetric\"\n    analysis: >\n      Value distribution 分析提供了更 fine-grained 的 overestimation 可视化，但不增加\n      nve 以外的 diagnostic 能力。对论文价值在于 \"illustration\" 而非 \"new finding\"。\n      可纳入 appendix 而非 main paper。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: \"Cosine similarity between dt=1 and dt=2 learned embeddings\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_cosine_5K: 0.92\n      walker_008d_cosine_35K: 0.88\n      walker_008d_cosine_55K: 0.85\n      walker_006_cosine_35K: 0.87\n      cosine_evolution_trend: \"slow decrease (0.92→0.85) — embeddings only weakly differentiated\"\n      cheetah_trained_cosine_35K: 0.91\n      cross_env_cosine_difference: \"minimal\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 cosine similarity 分析揭示一个反直觉结果：dt=1 和 dt=2 的 learned\n      embedding 高度相似（cosine 0.85-0.92），且 evolution 缓慢。这与 \"trained dt_emb\n      enables precise dt prediction in imagination\" 的叙事矛盾——如果 embedding 这么\n      相似，critic 如何利用它们区分 dt？可能的解释是 embedding 空间中的微小差异\n      （cosine 0.85 意味着 ~30° 角度差）足以让 MLP critic head 区分，但这削弱了\n      \"dt_embedding 是 smoking gun\" 的叙事力度——embedding 差异如此微小，可能只是\n      整个 RSSM 表征的一个次要信号，而非 primary driver。在 Cheetah 中 cosine\n      相似度与 Walker 几乎相同（0.91 vs 0.88），但 Cheetah 没有 collapse——进一步\n      说明 cosine similarity 不是 predictive 的。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"dt Embedding Cosine Similarity Evolution\"\n        columns: [\"environment\", \"config\", \"step\", \"cos(dt=1, dt=2)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker\", \"008d\", \"5K\", 0.92]\n          - [\"Walker\", \"008d\", \"35K\", 0.88]\n          - [\"Walker\", \"008d\", \"55K (collapse)\", 0.85]\n          - [\"Walker\", \"006\", \"35K\", 0.87]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", \"trained\", \"35K\", 0.91]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cosine similarity vs training step，Walker 和 Cheetah 叠加，差异极小\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cosine similarity 分析结果 inconclusive。embedding 差异微小且 cross-env 一致，\n      但 outcome 不同——说明 embedding 本身不是 causal bottleneck，RSSM fidelity 才是。\n      可放入 appendix 作为 \"embedding analysis does not explain cross-env differences\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_050\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in non-locomotion DMC environment\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 820\n      seed1_eval_105K: 795\n      seed2_eval_105K: 840\n      IQM_3seeds: 818\n      seed0_ve_35K: 0.22\n      seed0_ve_105K: 0.62\n      ve_stable_range: \"60-65% from 125K+\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole Swingup 是非 locomotion 环境，DreamerV3 baseline 应正常收敛。eval\n      在不同环境量级不同，Cartpole 可能在 800+ 范围收敛。v/e 校准与 Walker 和 Cheetah\n      又有不同（ve@35K ~0.22），为 cross-env 阈值统一增加第三个校准点的差异。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole Baseline\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"ve@35K\", \"ve@105K\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"seed 0\", 820, 0.22, 0.62]\n          - [\"seed 1\", 795, 0.20, 0.59]\n          - [\"seed 2\", 840, 0.24, 0.64]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole baseline 学习曲线\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 正常。v/e 校准位于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_051\"\n    description: \"Replicate delusional critic collapse in Cartpole Swingup\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 480\n      seed0_nve_peak: 1.20\n      seed0_nve_105K: 0.88\n      seed0_collapse: false\n      seed1_eval_105K: 510\n      seed1_nve_peak: 1.15\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 460\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.28\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      IQM_3seeds_105K: 483\n      IQM_pct_baseline: \"59%\"\n      nve_above_1_5x_count: \"0/3\"\n      collapse_count: \"0/3\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 Cheetah 相似的 non-replication。Cartpole Swingup 的 dynamics 虽然与 locomotion\n      不同（需要 swing + balance），但 RSSM 对 dt=2 步的预测误差仍然不够大到触发\n      delusional critic。obs_gap 预计约 1.45x（介于 Cheetah 的 1.35x 和 Walker 的 2.04x\n      之间），nve peak 约 1.15-1.28x，不达 1.5x 阈值。这是 worst 档最关键的证据——\n      两个独立的非 Walker 环境都不复现 nve>1.5x，证明 Walker 的 RSSM fidelity gap\n      是异常高的特例。cross_env_mechanism_replication 依然为 0。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole Trained dt_emb Results\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"% baseline\", \"nve peak\", \"collapse\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"seed 0\", 480, \"59%\", \"1.20x\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"seed 1\", 510, \"62%\", \"1.15x\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"seed 2\", 460, \"56%\", \"1.28x\", \"NO\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole nve 轨迹三 seed，全部低于 1.5x 阈值线\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cartpole 的 non-replication 与 Cheetah 形成合力，确认 \"nve>1.5x diagnostic\"\n      是 Walker-specific。C2 的 generalizability 为零。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_052\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control in Cartpole Swingup\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 465\n      seed0_nve_105K: 0.82\n      seed1_eval_105K: 490\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.90\n      seed2_eval_105K: 445\n      seed2_nve_105K: 0.85\n      IQM_3seeds_105K: 467\n      IQM_pct_baseline: \"57%\"\n      trained_vs_untrained_eval_gap: \"~3% (483 vs 467)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 Cheetah 相同的模式：trained vs untrained dt_emb 的差异极小（3%），因为 Cartpole\n      的 RSSM fidelity gap 不足以使 dt_emb 产生有意义的因果效应。degradation 主要\n      来自 subsample ON 的学习信号减少。两组的 nve 分布高度重叠（trained 0.88-1.28x\n      vs untrained 0.82-0.90x），不具 separating power。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole: Trained vs No dt_emb\"\n        columns: [\"config\", \"IQM eval@105K\", \"IQM nve@105K\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"trained dt_emb (051)\", 483, \"1.07x\"]\n          - [\"no dt_emb (052)\", 467, \"0.86x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole 两配置 nve violin plot，严重 overlap\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cartpole 确认 Cheetah 的发现：dt_emb 在低 RSSM-fidelity-gap 环境中无因果效应。\n\n  - name: \"Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_060\"\n    description: \"Pilot feasibility of RSSM-uncertainty-based imagination truncation\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_return_35K: 180\n      eval_return_45K: 210\n      eval_return_55K: 195\n      eval_return_65K: 170\n      eval_return_105K: 250\n      vs_baseline_105K: \"-73%\"\n      avg_imagination_length: 4.2\n      truncation_frequency: \"62% of rollouts truncated before H=15\"\n      nve_105K: 0.95\n      uncertainty_calibration: \"poor — std overestimates in early training, underestimates in late\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 uncertainty-gated truncation 的核心问题是 RSSM 的 uncertainty 估计\n      不可靠。DreamerV3 的 RSSM 使用 categorical latent（不是 Gaussian），其\n      uncertainty 没有 principled calibration。pilot 实现可能使用 ensemble disagreement\n      或 reconstruction error 作为 proxy，但这些 proxy 在 worst 档下表现不佳：\n      (1) 早期训练时 uncertainty 全面偏高，导致 rollout 过早截断（avg 仅 4.2 步，\n      vs H=15），学习信号极度不足；(2) 晚期训练时 RSSM 变得 overconfident，uncertainty\n      偏低，不再截断 — 但此时可能 dt=2 预测已经出现偏差。结果是 performance 仅\n      250@105K (27% baseline)，比 008d collapse (83@55K) 好但比 008a (778) 和 008e_v3\n      (870) 差很多。truncation 阈值难以 tune — 太紧学不了，太松不防崩。这使得\n      uncertainty-gated 方法在当前 RSSM 架构下不 feasible，削弱了 \"future work\"\n      方向的可信度。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Truncation Pilot Results\"\n        columns: [\"metric\", \"value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"eval@105K\", 250]\n          - [\"% baseline\", \"27%\"]\n          - [\"avg imagination length\", \"4.2 / 15 steps\"]\n          - [\"truncation rate\", \"62%\"]\n          - [\"nve@105K\", \"0.95x\"]\n          - [\"collapse\", \"NO\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Imagination length histogram at 35K vs 75K vs 105K，显示 truncation 行为随训练变化\"\n      - \"Uncertainty calibration plot: predicted uncertainty vs actual prediction error\"\n    analysis: >\n      Uncertainty-gated truncation 在 pilot 中不 feasible，主要因 RSSM uncertainty\n      calibration 差。不能作为 \"practical future direction\" 推荐，只能作为 \"open\n      challenge\" 讨论。论文的 actionable takeaway 进一步缩窄到 \"use dt=1 imagination\"\n      这一简单但 limited 的建议。\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: \"Third DMC locomotion environment for generalization\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_IQM: 250\n      trained_dt_emb_IQM: 145\n      trained_dt_emb_pct_baseline: \"58%\"\n      trained_dt_emb_nve_peak_range: \"[1.10, 1.35]\"\n      trained_dt_emb_collapse_count: \"0/3\"\n      no_dt_emb_IQM: 138\n      no_dt_emb_pct_baseline: \"55%\"\n      trained_vs_untrained_gap: \"~5%\"\n      cross_env_replication: 0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Hopper Hop 作为第三个 locomotion 环境，在 worst 档下与 Cheetah 表现一致——\n      trained dt_emb 不触发 nve>1.5x，无 collapse。Hopper 的 dynamics 虽然比 Cheetah\n      更非线性（hopping requires contact dynamics），但 RSSM 的 dt=2 预测误差仍不足\n      以触发正反馈 loop（预计 obs_gap ~1.55x，低于 Walker 的 2.04x）。degradation\n      pattern 是 uniform 的 plateau（~58% baseline），trained vs untrained dt_emb 差异\n      仅 ~5%。三个非 Walker 环境（Cheetah, Cartpole, Hopper）统一不复现，确认\n      Walker 的 delusional critic 是 environment-specific outlier。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Hopper Hop Summary\"\n        columns: [\"config\", \"IQM eval@105K\", \"% baseline\", \"nve peak\", \"collapse\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"baseline\", 250, \"100%\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", 145, \"58%\", \"1.25x\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"no dt_emb\", 138, \"55%\", \"0.90x\", \"0/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Hopper 三配置 bar chart with error bars\"\n    analysis: >\n      Hopper 进一步巩固 non-replication 结论。四个环境中仅 Walker 展示 delusional critic。\n\n  # ---- Cross-cutting summary metrics for worst tier ----\n\n  - name: \"Worst Tier Aggregate Assessment\"\n    plan_id: \"aggregate\"\n    description: \"Cross-experiment summary metrics defining the worst tier\"\n    expected_results:\n      C6_recovery_pct_of_baseline: 73\n      nve_threshold_classification_accuracy: 0.67\n      cross_env_mechanism_replication: 0\n      collapse_prob_trained_dt_emb: 0.11\n      walker_008e_v3_IQM_pct_baseline: 73\n      walker_nve_separating_power: 0.67\n      total_collapse_events: \"1/9 (Walker 008d s0 only)\"\n      environments_with_nve_above_1_5x: \"1/4 (Walker only, 2/3 seeds)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      跨所有实验的聚合视图。collapse 概率 1/9 = 11%（9 个 trained dt_emb seed 中仅 1 个\n      collapse：Walker 008d seed 0）。nve>1.5x 仅在 Walker 中出现（2/3 seeds），其他\n      三个环境（Cheetah 0/3, Cartpole 0/3, Hopper 0/3）无一超过。1.5x 阈值在 Walker\n      内部的 classification accuracy 为 4/6 = 67%（trained 2/3 exceed + untrained\n      008f s1 1/3 也 exceed）。C6 mitigation 的 cross-seed IQM 仅 73%。\n      这些数字共同指向一个结论：原来的 \"universal diagnostic mechanism\" 叙事不成立，\n      论文必须 reframe 为 \"Walker-specific case study + diagnostic methodology contribution\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-Environment Mechanism Summary\"\n        columns: [\"environment\", \"trained dt_emb nve>1.5x\", \"collapse\", \"untrained nve>1.5x\", \"dt_emb causal effect\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"2/3 (67%)\", \"1/3 (33%)\", \"1/3 (33%)\", \"moderate\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"negligible\"]\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"negligible\"]\n          - [\"Hopper Hop\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"negligible\"]\n          - [\"TOTAL\", \"2/12 (17%)\", \"1/12 (8%)\", \"1/12 (8%)\", \"—\"]\n      - name: \"Paper Claim Viability Under Worst Tier\"\n        columns: [\"claim\", \"original strength\", \"worst tier strength\", \"reframe needed\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"C1 (degradation)\", \"Strong\", \"Strong\", \"NO — all configs degrade everywhere\"]\n          - [\"C2 (nve>1.5x diagnostic)\", \"Moderate-strong\", \"Weak\", \"YES — Walker-only, classification 67%\"]\n          - [\"C3 (value suppression)\", \"Strong\", \"Moderate\", \"YES — direction holds, magnitude varies\"]\n          - [\"C4 (dt amplification)\", \"Moderate\", \"Moderate\", \"NO — still only 2 dt values\"]\n          - [\"C5 (horizon/subsample)\", \"Moderate\", \"Moderate-strong\", \"YES — becomes PRIMARY factor in Cheetah\"]\n          - [\"C6 (mitigation)\", \"Moderate-strong\", \"Weak-moderate\", \"YES — 73% IQM, high variance\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Hero figure: 4-environment × 3-config heatmap of nve peak, with 1.5x threshold contour showing Walker isolation\"\n      - \"Forest plot: C6 mitigation % baseline across seeds and environments with CI\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档下论文的可行叙事：(1) C1 保持不变（degradation is universal）；(2) C2 降级\n      为 Walker case study，但 reframe 为 \"failure mode is architecture×environment\n      interaction\"；(3) C5 升级为 Cheetah/Cartpole/Hopper 的 primary explanatory\n      factor（learning signal reduction, not delusional critic）；(4) RSSM fidelity table\n      作为核心方法论贡献，解释 why failure modes differ across environments；\n      (5) C6 降级为 environment-conditional guideline。标题改为问句形式：\n      \"When Does Temporal Abstraction Break World Models?\"——承认答案是 conditional。\n      CoRL 预期 borderline：methodology novelty（factorial ablation + nve protocol）\n      可能获得一个审稿人的认可，但 lack of generalizable findings 会被另一个审稿人\n      视为 insufficient contribution。补充 plan_032 的 value distribution 分析可增加\n      分析深度但不改变核心问题。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":308,"cache_read_input_tokens":42241,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":308},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0c2338d-48fd-4569-bbff-a85af5e5ab47","uuid":"cee1e6eb-87ae-4931-9f16-a86fb499c9fb"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":450543,"duration_api_ms":452935,"num_turns":2,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心reframe：从\"诊断temporal abstraction的通用失败机制\"转向\"DreamerV3 RSSM fidelity\n  作为temporal abstraction的瓶颈——一个受控案例研究\"。主贡献从diagnostic finding变为\n  diagnostic methodology（factorial ablation框架 + nve监控协议）。将non-replication\n  本身作为finding——\"temporal abstraction的失败模式是architecture×environment交互的产物，\n  不存在universal failure mode\"。C6降级为environment-conditional guideline。\n  标题候选：\"When Does Temporal Abstraction Break World Models? An Empirical\n  Investigation of DreamerV3\"。CoRL审稿预期：borderline。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"2 additional seeds for baseline v/e calibration\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_009d_eval_return_105K: 908\n      seed1_009d_eval_return_last10_mean: 935\n      seed1_009d_ve_ratio_35K: 0.215\n      seed1_009d_ve_ratio_45K: 0.305\n      seed1_009d_ve_ratio_105K: 0.635\n      seed1_009d_ve_stable: \"67-71% from 135K+\"\n      seed2_009a_eval_return_105K: 919\n      seed2_009a_eval_return_last10_mean: 942\n      seed2_009a_ve_ratio_35K: 0.248\n      seed2_009a_ve_ratio_105K: 0.699\n      seed2_009a_ve_stable: \"69-71% from 245K+\"\n      IQM_baseline_3seeds_105K: 916\n      cross_seed_std_eval_105K: 12.3\n      cross_seed_ve_35K_range: \"[0.215, 0.248]\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Baseline (dt=1) 本身不受 worst 档影响——它是标准 DreamerV3 在 Walker Walk 的收敛行为，\n      三个 seed 均应收敛到 900-960 范围。但 worst 档的隐患在于 v/e 校准的 seed 间变异：\n      seed 1 的 ve_ratio@35K 可能偏低至 0.215（vs seed 0 的 0.241），这意味着以 seed 0\n      校准的 1.5x 阈值（即绝对 v/e=0.362）在 seed 1 的背景下实际对应 1.68x normalized，\n      引入 ~12% 的阈值偏移。这不影响 baseline 本身的结论，但会在后续 nve 计算中放大噪声，\n      为 cross-seed 的 threshold 可靠性埋下问题。seed 2 (009a) 已确认收敛正常。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Walker Baseline Cross-Seed Summary\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"ve@35K\", \"ve@105K\", \"ve_stable\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"seed 0 (001)\", 916, 0.241, 0.656, \"69-72%\"]\n          - [\"seed 1 (009d)\", 908, 0.215, 0.635, \"67-71%\"]\n          - [\"seed 2 (009a)\", 919, 0.248, 0.699, \"69-71%\"]\n          - [\"IQM ± CI\", \"916 ± 14\", \"0.235 ± 0.017\", \"0.663 ± 0.033\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三 seed baseline 学习曲线叠加图，eval return vs step，显示紧密收敛 band\"\n      - \"三 seed v/e ratio vs step，标注 35K 处各 seed 的校准值差异\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 本身稳健，但 v/e@35K 的 15% cross-seed 变异意味着 nve=1.5x 阈值在\n      不同 seed 组合下对应不同的绝对 v/e 水平。在 worst 档中这个变异被放大——当 Cheetah/Cartpole\n      的 baseline v/e 校准可能与 Walker 差异更大时，统一阈值的 cross-env 可靠性进一步下降。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"Replicate delusional critic collapse with 2 more seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed2_009b_status: \"DONE — no collapse, transient nve>1.5x\"\n      seed2_009b_eval_105K: 268\n      seed2_009b_nve_peak: 2.05\n      seed2_009b_nve_peak_step: \"25K (early, before baseline v/e converges)\"\n      seed2_009b_nve_45K: 1.62\n      seed2_009b_nve_105K: 0.38\n      seed2_009b_collapse: false\n      seed1_009e_eval_25K: 155\n      seed1_009e_eval_35K: 178\n      seed1_009e_eval_45K: 192\n      seed1_009e_eval_55K: 175\n      seed1_009e_eval_105K: 215\n      seed1_009e_nve_25K: 1.45\n      seed1_009e_nve_35K: 1.35\n      seed1_009e_nve_45K: 1.28\n      seed1_009e_nve_55K: 1.15\n      seed1_009e_nve_105K: 0.82\n      seed1_009e_collapse: false\n      collapse_count_of_3: \"1/3 (33%)\"\n      nve_above_1_5x_at_35Kplus: \"2/3 (008d seed 0, 009b seed 2)\"\n      nve_threshold_classification_accuracy: 0.67\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档核心预测：009e (seed 1) 的 nve 在 35K+ 始终不超过 1.5x。机制：trained dt_emb\n      的 delusional critic 效应依赖 RSSM 在 dt=2 时的预测偏差方向——如果 seed 1 的初始化\n      恰好让 RSSM 在 dt=2 时产生偏保守（而非偏乐观）的 reward 预测，trained dt_emb 的\n      conditioning 反而会让 value function 低估（不是高估）dt=2 trajectory 的价值。\n      009e 的 nve@25K=1.45x（接近但未达 1.5x），然后随训练进行单调下降至 0.82x@105K。\n      这意味着 1.5x 阈值在 trained dt_emb 组的分类能力降至 2/3（不再是 2/2），总体\n      classification accuracy 从 4/4=100% 降至 4/6=67%。009b@25K 的 2.05x 本身是\n      early false positive（baseline v/e 仅 0.087 时比率不稳定），在 35K+ 仅有\n      45K 的 1.62x 真正可靠。collapse 概率仅 1/3=33%，且唯一的 collapse（008d seed 0）\n      仅在 H=8 配置下观察到。如果 009e 也是 H=8 配置但不 collapse，进一步说明\n      collapse 是高度随机的罕见事件，而非 trained dt_emb 的确定性后果。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008d Config Cross-Seed nve Trajectory\"\n        columns: [\"step\", \"seed 0 (008d) nve\", \"seed 1 (009e) nve\", \"seed 2 (009b) nve\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"25K\", \"1.78*\", \"1.45*\", \"2.05*\"]\n          - [\"35K\", \"1.71\", \"1.35\", \"1.24\"]\n          - [\"45K\", \"2.09\", \"1.28\", \"1.62\"]\n          - [\"55K\", \"4.12 → collapse\", \"1.15\", \"1.41\"]\n          - [\"105K\", \"collapsed\", \"0.82\", \"0.38\"]\n        note: \"*25K values unreliable due to low baseline v/e (0.087)\"\n      - name: \"1.5x Threshold Classification (Updated)\"\n        columns: [\"group\", \"seed\", \"nve>1.5x at 35K+?\", \"collapse?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", \"008d s0\", \"YES (sustained)\", \"YES\"]\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", \"009e s1\", \"NO (peak 1.35)\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", \"009b s2\", \"YES (transient)\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"no dt_emb\", \"008f s0\", \"NO (peak 1.02)\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"no dt_emb\", \"009f s1\", \"YES (1.52x@95K)\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"no dt_emb\", \"009c s2\", \"NO (peak 1.26)\", \"NO\"]\n        note: \"Classification accuracy drops to 4/6 = 67%\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三 seed nve 轨迹叠加图，1.5x 阈值线标注，显示 seed 1 始终在阈值下方\"\n      - \"eval return 三 seed 叠加，仅 seed 0 展示 collapse pattern\"\n    analysis: >\n      009e 不超过 1.5x 阈值直接削弱 C2 的 \"reliable diagnostic marker\" 定位。\n      nve>1.5x 不再是 trained dt_emb 的确定性后果，而是概率性后果（~67% 的 seed 会触发）。\n      更关键的是 collapse 概率仅 1/3——即使 nve 超过 1.5x（如 009b），系统也能\n      自我纠正。论文中必须承认 \"nve>1.5x is a risk indicator, not a deterministic\n      predictor\"，这显著削弱了诊断价值的叙事。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control stability with 2 more seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed2_009c_status: \"DONE — decline to 148@105K, nve=1.14x\"\n      seed2_009c_eval_105K: 148\n      seed2_009c_nve_105K: 1.14\n      seed2_009c_trend: \"decline after 75K peak\"\n      seed1_009f_eval_25K: 175\n      seed1_009f_eval_35K: 195\n      seed1_009f_eval_45K: 210\n      seed1_009f_eval_55K: 188\n      seed1_009f_eval_65K: 230\n      seed1_009f_eval_75K: 265\n      seed1_009f_eval_85K: 285\n      seed1_009f_eval_95K: 310\n      seed1_009f_eval_105K: 275\n      seed1_009f_nve_35K: 0.85\n      seed1_009f_nve_45K: 0.92\n      seed1_009f_nve_55K: 1.08\n      seed1_009f_nve_65K: 1.22\n      seed1_009f_nve_75K: 1.38\n      seed1_009f_nve_85K: 1.45\n      seed1_009f_nve_95K: 1.52\n      seed1_009f_nve_105K: 1.35\n      seed1_009f_nve_crosses_1_5x: true\n      untrained_group_nve_above_1_5x: \"1/3 seeds (009f)\"\n      causal_control_reliability: \"compromised\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档核心问题之一：009c 已确认 008f 的保护不 robust（decline to 148，nve=1.14x\n      且上升趋势）。009f 在 worst 档下进一步恶化——nve 在 95K 触及 1.52x（超过 1.5x 阈值），\n      尽管随后回落至 1.35x。机制：dt_embed_dim=0 去掉了 dt conditioning，但 RSSM 仍然\n      隐式学习了 dt=1/dt=2 的状态转移差异（通过观察到的 state transition 模式）。在某些\n      seed 中，这种隐式学习足以让 value function 逐渐开发出对 dt>1 trajectory 的偏好，\n      只是速度比 trained dt_emb 慢得多（008f s1@95K 才达到 1.52x vs 008d s0@35K 就达到\n      1.71x）。这意味着 dt_embedding 是 amplifier 但不是 sole enabler——RSSM 本身在\n      长时间训练后也能产生类似（但更弱的）效应。这直接削弱了 \"dt_embedding is the\n      necessary and sufficient cause\" 的因果声明。009c 的 decline pattern 与 009f 的\n      borderline nve 共同表明 008f 不是可靠的 causal control——\"eliminates\" 和\n      \"significantly delays\" 都过强，实际效果是 \"partially attenuates with high\n      seed-dependent variance\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008f Config Cross-Seed Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"metric\", \"seed 0 (008f)\", \"seed 1 (009f)\", \"seed 2 (009c)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"eval@105K\", 503, 275, 148]\n          - [\"nve peak (35K+)\", \"0.97x@55K\", \"1.52x@95K\", \"1.14x@105K\"]\n          - [\"nve@105K\", \"0.30x\", \"1.35x\", \"1.14x\"]\n          - [\"trend\", \"zigzag recovery\", \"slow rise then mild decline\", \"peak-then-decline\"]\n          - [\"nve>1.5x?\", \"NO\", \"YES (transient)\", \"NO\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"008f 三 seed eval + nve 叠加图，显示极高 cross-seed variance（503 vs 275 vs 148）\"\n      - \"与 008d 三 seed 对比：nve 分布 overlap 区域标注\"\n    analysis: >\n      008f 三 seed 的 eval@105K 范围为 148-503（3.4x 差异），cross-seed variance 极大，\n      使其作为 causal control 不可靠。更严重的是 009f 的 nve 突破 1.5x，意味着\n      untrained/no-dt-emb 组也存在 nve>1.5x 的 seed——阈值的 separating power 从 4/4\n      降至 4/6 (67%)，不再具有 \"perfect classification\" 的论文叙事价值。C2 的因果声明\n      必须软化为 \"trained dt_emb significantly increases the probability and speed\n      of pathological overestimation, but does not exclusively cause it\"。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 (mitigation) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"Multi-seed validation of dt=1 imagination mitigation\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 870\n      seed0_nve_105K: 0.80\n      seed1_eval_25K: 142\n      seed1_eval_35K: 225\n      seed1_eval_45K: 310\n      seed1_eval_55K: 380\n      seed1_eval_65K: 425\n      seed1_eval_75K: 460\n      seed1_eval_85K: 495\n      seed1_eval_95K: 540\n      seed1_eval_105K: 590\n      seed1_nve_35K: 0.98\n      seed1_nve_45K: 0.95\n      seed1_nve_55K: 0.92\n      seed1_nve_65K: 0.85\n      seed1_nve_75K: 0.82\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.88\n      seed1_vs_baseline_105K: \"-35.6%\"\n      seed2_eval_25K: 135\n      seed2_eval_35K: 210\n      seed2_eval_45K: 285\n      seed2_eval_55K: 350\n      seed2_eval_65K: 390\n      seed2_eval_75K: 440\n      seed2_eval_85K: 480\n      seed2_eval_95K: 510\n      seed2_eval_105K: 550\n      seed2_nve_35K: 1.02\n      seed2_nve_45K: 0.96\n      seed2_nve_55K: 0.90\n      seed2_nve_65K: 0.88\n      seed2_nve_75K: 0.85\n      seed2_nve_105K: 0.91\n      seed2_vs_baseline_105K: \"-40.0%\"\n      IQM_3seeds_eval_105K: 670\n      IQM_3seeds_pct_baseline: 73\n      cross_seed_std: 173\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档核心假设：C6 的 95% baseline recovery 是 seed-specific 的幸运结果。\n      seed 0 的 870 可能是因为其初始化恰好让 RSSM 在 dt=1 imagination 下产生了与\n      pure baseline 接近的训练信号分布。seed 1 和 seed 2 可能面临不同的问题：\n      subsample ON 意味着训练数据包含 dt=2 transitions，这些 transition 的 RSSM 表征\n      即使在 dt=1 imagination 时也会 \"污染\" latent state 的学习。在某些 seed 中，\n      这种污染效应更明显——RSSM 对 dt=2 transition 分配了更多 representational capacity，\n      导致 dt=1 imagination 的 rollout quality 反而下降。结果是 seed 1 仅达 590\n      (64% baseline)，seed 2 仅达 550 (60% baseline)。IQM 约 670 (73% baseline)，\n      远低于 seed 0 的 95%。nve 保持健康（0.85-1.02x），但 performance 本身不够。\n      在 worst 档下，C6 从 \"practical zero-cost mitigation (95% recovery)\" 降级为\n      \"environment-conditional partial mitigation (58-95% recovery, high variance)\"，\n      显著削弱 actionable takeaway 的说服力。论文中 008e_v3 不能作为推荐方案呈现，\n      只能作为 \"one possible direction\" 附带 high-variance caveat。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008e_v3 Mitigation Cross-Seed Results\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"% baseline\", \"nve@105K\", \"collapse?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"seed 0\", 870, \"95%\", \"0.80x\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"seed 1\", 590, \"64%\", \"0.88x\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"seed 2\", 550, \"60%\", \"0.91x\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"IQM ± CI\", \"670 ± 185\", \"73% ± 20%\", \"0.86x ± 0.06\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"008e_v3 三 seed 学习曲线叠加，seed 0 远高于 seed 1/2，显示 recovery 的 seed-dependence\"\n      - \"与 baseline 三 seed 对比的 IQM bar chart，error bar 显示巨大 CI\"\n    analysis: >\n      C6 recovery 的 IQM 73% 落入 worst 档指标范围 [58,82]。20pp CI 使得\n      \"practical mitigation\" 的叙事站不住——审稿人会质疑 \"a mitigation that recovers\n      60-95% depending on seed is not actionable\"。必须 reframe 为 conditional\n      guideline，强调 dt=1 imagination 至少避免 collapse（三 seed 无一 collapse，\n      nve 均健康），即使 performance recovery 不一致。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression with 2 more seeds\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_55K: 420\n      seed1_eval_65K: 380\n      seed1_eval_75K: 350\n      seed1_eval_85K: 390\n      seed1_eval_95K: 410\n      seed1_eval_105K: 450\n      seed1_nve_55K: 0.85\n      seed1_nve_65K: 0.72\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.68\n      seed1_pattern: \"single weak V-recovery, lower amplitude than seed 0\"\n      seed2_eval_55K: 350\n      seed2_eval_65K: 310\n      seed2_eval_75K: 340\n      seed2_eval_85K: 360\n      seed2_eval_95K: 330\n      seed2_eval_105K: 380\n      seed2_nve_55K: 0.88\n      seed2_nve_65K: 0.78\n      seed2_nve_105K: 0.75\n      seed2_pattern: \"oscillating plateau, no clear V-recovery\"\n      IQM_3seeds_105K: 536\n      IQM_pct_baseline: \"59%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      seed 0 的 778@105K (85% baseline) 和 double V-recovery pattern 在 worst 档下\n      不被 replicate。原因：untrained dt_emb 的保护依赖于 random embedding 恰好不与\n      RSSM 的 dt=2 状态表征 align——如果 random initialization 碰巧与某个有意义的\n      dt-相关方向 partially aligned，保护效果减弱。seed 1 展示弱化版 V-recovery\n      （amplitude 更小，peak 仅 450 vs seed 0 的 778），seed 2 则表现为无方向性的\n      oscillating plateau（330-380 范围）。nve 仍保持在 baseline 以下（0.68-0.88x），\n      确认 value growth suppression 的方向性成立，但 performance recovery 的幅度\n      高度 seed-dependent。C3 的 \"substantive protection\" 声明在 IQM 仅 59% baseline\n      的情况下需要大幅软化。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008a Untrained dt_emb Cross-Seed Summary\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"% baseline\", \"nve@105K\", \"pattern\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"seed 0\", 778, \"85%\", \"0.59x\", \"double V-recovery\"]\n          - [\"seed 1\", 450, \"49%\", \"0.68x\", \"weak single V-recovery\"]\n          - [\"seed 2\", 380, \"41%\", \"0.75x\", \"oscillating plateau\"]\n          - [\"IQM\", 536, \"59%\", \"0.67x\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三 seed eval 轨迹叠加，seed 0 的 V-recovery pattern 在其他 seed 中不复现\"\n    analysis: >\n      nve suppression 方向一致（三 seed 均 <1.0x），但 performance recovery 差异巨大。\n      C3 需要 rewrite：\"untrained dt_emb reliably suppresses value growth below baseline\n      levels, but performance recovery is highly variable (41-85% baseline)\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in second DMC environment\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 720\n      seed1_eval_105K: 695\n      seed2_eval_105K: 740\n      IQM_3seeds: 718\n      seed0_ve_35K: 0.185\n      seed0_ve_105K: 0.58\n      seed1_ve_35K: 0.170\n      seed2_ve_35K: 0.195\n      ve_stable_range: \"55-62% from 135K+\"\n      convergence_step: \"~85K (faster than Walker's ~135K)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah Run baseline 应正常收敛——DreamerV3 在此环境有良好 track record。但\n      v/e 校准值与 Walker 显著不同：Cheetah 的 ve@35K 约 0.18（vs Walker 的 0.24），\n      ve 收敛更快（~85K vs ~135K），stable range 更低（55-62% vs 69-72%）。这种\n      环境间的 v/e 校准差异意味着 Walker 中 calibrated 的 1.5x nve 阈值在 Cheetah\n      中对应不同的绝对 v/e 水平（0.18×1.5=0.27 vs Walker 的 0.24×1.5=0.36），\n      使 cross-env 阈值统一变得更复杂。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah Run Baseline\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"ve@35K\", \"ve@105K\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"seed 0\", 720, 0.185, 0.58]\n          - [\"seed 1\", 695, 0.170, 0.56]\n          - [\"seed 2\", 740, 0.195, 0.61]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah baseline 三 seed 学习曲线，与 Walker baseline 对比标注收敛速度差异\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 正常但 v/e 校准差异为后续 cross-env nve 比较制造了 confound。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: \"Replicate delusional critic collapse in Cheetah Run\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_35K: 385\n      seed0_eval_45K: 410\n      seed0_eval_55K: 395\n      seed0_eval_65K: 380\n      seed0_eval_105K: 420\n      seed0_nve_35K: 1.15\n      seed0_nve_45K: 1.22\n      seed0_nve_55K: 1.18\n      seed0_nve_105K: 0.95\n      seed0_collapse: false\n      seed1_eval_105K: 380\n      seed1_nve_peak: 1.30\n      seed1_nve_105K: 1.05\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 350\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.25\n      seed2_nve_105K: 1.10\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      IQM_3seeds_105K: 383\n      IQM_pct_baseline: \"53%\"\n      nve_above_1_5x_count: \"0/3\"\n      collapse_count: \"0/3\"\n      cross_env_mechanism_replication: 0\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档核心预测：Cheetah Run 中 trained dt_emb 不触发 nve>1.5x。原因：\n      Cheetah Run 的 RSSM 在 dt=2 的预测质量比 Walker Walk 更好——Cheetah 的\n      dynamics 更平滑（近似线性 forward motion），RSSM 的 dt=2 预测误差更小（预计\n      obs_gap ~1.4x vs Walker 的 2.04x）。更低的 RSSM fidelity gap 意味着 trained\n      dt_emb 的 conditioning 虽然精确，但它 condition 的目标（dt=2 predictions）\n      与真实 dynamics 的偏差更小——value function 的 overestimation 被限制在 1.1-1.3x\n      范围，不足以触发正反馈 loop。performance 仍然 degraded（53% baseline），但\n      degradation 模式是 \"slow plateau\" 而非 \"delusional critic collapse\"。\n      这直接证明 Walker 中观察到的 nve>1.5x → collapse 机制是 environment-specific\n      的：它依赖于 RSSM 在特定环境的 dt=2 预测误差大小，而非 trained dt_emb 的\n      universal 效应。三个 seed 无一超过 1.5x，cross_env_mechanism_replication = 0。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah Trained dt_emb Results\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"% baseline\", \"nve peak (35K+)\", \"nve@105K\", \"collapse\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"seed 0\", 420, \"58%\", \"1.22x@45K\", \"0.95x\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"seed 1\", 380, \"53%\", \"1.30x@55K\", \"1.05x\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"seed 2\", 350, \"49%\", \"1.25x@45K\", \"1.10x\", \"NO\"]\n      - name: \"Cross-Environment nve>1.5x Summary\"\n        columns: [\"environment\", \"trained dt_emb seeds exceeding 1.5x\", \"collapse seeds\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"2/3 (67%)\", \"1/3 (33%)\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah vs Walker nve 轨迹对比图：Walker 展示 >1.5x 发散，Cheetah 稳定在 1.0-1.3x\"\n      - \"Cheetah eval 学习曲线（三 seed），无 collapse pattern，仅 plateau degradation\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 的 non-replication 是 worst 档最具杀伤力的发现。它证明 \"trained dt_emb\n      → nve>1.5x → collapse\" 不是 universal mechanism，而是 environment-conditional。\n      论文叙事必须 reframe：delusional critic 的触发条件是 \"sufficient RSSM fidelity\n      gap at dt>1\"，这在不同环境中可能满足也可能不满足。C2 从 \"trained dt_emb\n      reliably triggers pathological overestimation\" 变为 \"trained dt_emb amplifies\n      RSSM fidelity gap into overestimation, with magnitude depending on\n      environment-specific prediction difficulty at dt>1\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control in Cheetah Run\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 390\n      seed0_nve_105K: 0.88\n      seed1_eval_105K: 370\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.95\n      seed2_eval_105K: 355\n      seed2_nve_105K: 1.02\n      IQM_3seeds_105K: 372\n      IQM_pct_baseline: \"52%\"\n      nve_above_1_5x_count: \"0/3\"\n      trained_vs_untrained_eval_gap: \"~3% (383 vs 372)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cheetah 中 trained dt_emb (plan_021) 和 no-dt_emb (plan_022) 的 performance\n      差异极小（383 vs 372，~3%），远小于 Walker 中的差异（008d collapse vs 008f 503）。\n      原因：Cheetah 中 RSSM fidelity gap 本身就小，所以 dt_emb 的有无对结果影响不大——\n      degradation 主要来自 subsample ON 导致的学习信号减少和 shorter effective horizon，\n      而非 delusional critic。nve 保持在 0.88-1.02x 范围，与 plan_021 的 0.95-1.10x\n      高度重叠。这意味着在 Cheetah 中，dt_emb 作为因果变量几乎无 separating power——\n      trained vs untrained 的 nve 分布 overlap 严重。C2 的因果论证在 Cheetah 中\n      完全不成立。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah: Trained vs No dt_emb Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"config\", \"IQM eval@105K\", \"IQM nve@105K\", \"gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"trained dt_emb (021)\", 383, \"1.03x\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"no dt_emb (022)\", 372, \"0.95x\", \"~3% eval, 0.08x nve\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah trained vs untrained dt_emb 的 nve 分布 violin plot，显示完全 overlap\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 中 dt_emb 因果效应接近零。degradation 是 uniform 的，不区分 trained/untrained。\n      这进一步支持 \"Walker-specific mechanism\" 结论。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression in Cheetah Run\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 520\n      seed1_eval_105K: 490\n      seed2_eval_105K: 540\n      IQM_3seeds_105K: 517\n      IQM_pct_baseline: \"72%\"\n      seed0_nve_105K: 0.78\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.85\n      seed2_nve_105K: 0.72\n      v_recovery_pattern: \"gradual improvement, no distinct V-shape\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      subsample OFF 在 Cheetah 中带来更多训练数据，performance 提升至 72% baseline\n      （vs subsample ON 的 52-53%）。但 Cheetah 中没有 delusional critic 问题（因 RSSM\n      fidelity gap 小），所以 untrained dt_emb 的 \"value suppression\" 效应无从体现——\n      nve 在 0.72-0.85x 范围，但 trained dt_emb 组也在 0.95-1.10x（无 pathological），\n      两组的 nve 差异远小于 Walker（Walker 中 untrained 0.59-0.93x vs trained 1.71-4.12x，\n      差异巨大；Cheetah 中 untrained 0.72-0.85x vs trained 0.95-1.10x，差异仅 0.2x）。\n      C3 的 \"preventing optimistic drift\" 在 Cheetah 中不具意义——因为 trained dt_emb\n      本身就不产生 optimistic drift。学习曲线呈现渐进上升而非 Walker 的 V-recovery，\n      进一步说明 Walker 的 zigzag pattern 是 environment-specific 的 transient dynamics。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah Untrained dt_emb (no subsample)\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"% baseline\", \"nve@105K\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"seed 0\", 520, \"72%\", \"0.78x\"]\n          - [\"seed 1\", 490, \"68%\", \"0.85x\"]\n          - [\"seed 2\", 540, \"75%\", \"0.72x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah 四配置（baseline, trained, no-dt-emb, untrained-no-subsample）IQM bar chart\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 中 subsample ON/OFF 的效应（52% vs 72%）大于 dt_emb trained/untrained\n      的效应（~3%），说明在此环境中 primary degradation factor 是 learning signal\n      reduction，不是 delusional critic。与 Walker 的因果结构完全不同。\n\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: \"Quantify RSSM fidelity gap across models\"\n    expected_results:\n      cheetah_baseline_obs_gap: 1.35\n      cheetah_baseline_reward_gap: 1.18\n      cheetah_008d_obs_gap: 1.25\n      cheetah_008d_reward_gap: 1.85\n      cheetah_008f_obs_gap: 1.40\n      cheetah_008f_reward_gap: 1.02\n      walker_vs_cheetah_obs_gap_ratio: \"2.04x / 1.35x = Walker fidelity gap 51% larger\"\n      cartpole_baseline_obs_gap: 1.20\n      cross_env_fidelity_gap_correlation_with_collapse: \"weak (r ≈ 0.45)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 RSSM fidelity 分析揭示一个尴尬事实：Walker 的 obs_gap (2.04x) 远高于\n      Cheetah (1.35x) 和 Cartpole (1.20x)。这解释了为什么 delusional critic 仅在\n      Walker 中触发——RSSM 在 Walker 的 dt=2 步预测质量显著更差。但这也意味着 \"RSSM\n      fidelity gap → delusional critic\" 的因果链虽然在方向上成立（gap 大 → 更容易\n      overestimate），但 gap 的大小是 environment-specific 的，无法预先判断哪个环境会\n      触发。Cheetah 中 trained dt_emb 的 reward_gap (1.85x) 虽然高于 baseline (1.18x)，\n      但远低于 Walker 008d 的 2.78x——不足以驱动正反馈 loop。fidelity gap 与 collapse\n      的相关性较弱（r≈0.45），因为中间变量太多（seed 随机性、training dynamics、\n      environment reward structure）。RSSM fidelity table 升级为核心贡献的叙事方向\n      在 worst 档下是对的，但贡献从 \"predictive tool\" 降级为 \"post-hoc explanatory\n      framework\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-Environment RSSM Fidelity Gap\"\n        columns: [\"environment\", \"config\", \"obs_gap (dt2/dt1)\", \"reward_gap\", \"collapse?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker\", \"baseline\", \"2.04x\", \"1.56x\", \"N/A\"]\n          - [\"Walker\", \"trained dt_emb\", \"1.30x*\", \"2.78x\", \"1/3 seeds\"]\n          - [\"Walker\", \"no dt_emb\", \"2.75x\", \"1.01x\", \"0/3 seeds\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", \"baseline\", \"1.35x\", \"1.18x\", \"N/A\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", \"trained dt_emb\", \"1.25x\", \"1.85x\", \"0/3 seeds\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", \"no dt_emb\", \"1.40x\", \"1.02x\", \"0/3 seeds\"]\n        note: \"*Walker 008d obs_gap 低因模型已整体崩塌（dt=1 绝对误差 3x baseline）\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-env RSSM fidelity gap scatter plot: obs_gap vs nve_peak，标注 Walker vs Cheetah 的分离\"\n    analysis: >\n      Fidelity gap 解释了 cross-env 差异但不预测它。论文中 RSSM fidelity table 作为\n      \"post-hoc diagnostic\"，价值有限——审稿人会问 \"how do I know a priori if my\n      environment has sufficient fidelity gap to worry about delusional critic?\"\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: \"Plot actor entropy for healthy vs collapsed configs\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_s0_entropy_35K: 3.2\n      walker_008d_s0_entropy_45K: 2.8\n      walker_008d_s0_entropy_55K: 2.1\n      walker_008d_s0_pattern: \"monotonic decrease even during collapse\"\n      walker_008a_s0_entropy_55K: 3.5\n      walker_008a_s0_entropy_105K: 3.1\n      walker_baseline_entropy_55K: 3.8\n      walker_baseline_entropy_105K: 3.0\n      entropy_separation: \"weak — collapsed config shows lower entropy but overlaps with late-training baseline\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 actor entropy 分析不产生 clean separation。预期 collapsed 配置（008d）\n      的 entropy 在 collapse 前单调下降——这看起来像是 policy 过度确信而非困惑，但\n      baseline 在晚期训练中也展示 entropy 下降（3.8→3.0），使得区分变得模糊。\n      008d 的 entropy 在 55K (collapse 时) 约 2.1，而 baseline@55K 约 3.8（差异明显），\n      但 008d@35K=3.2 与 baseline@95K=3.2 完全重合——如果不知道 step 信息，无法仅凭\n      entropy 值判断是否即将 collapse。entropy 不是一个可用的 early warning signal，\n      削弱了将其作为 diagnostic metric 的价值。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Actor Entropy Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"config\", \"step\", \"actor_entropy\", \"eval_return\", \"status\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"008d s0\", \"35K\", 3.2, 146, \"pre-collapse\"]\n          - [\"008d s0\", \"55K\", 2.1, 83, \"collapsed\"]\n          - [\"baseline\", \"35K\", 4.1, 389, \"healthy\"]\n          - [\"baseline\", \"55K\", 3.8, 626, \"healthy\"]\n          - [\"baseline\", \"95K\", 3.2, 920, \"converged\"]\n          - [\"008a s0\", \"55K\", 3.5, 488, \"V-recovery dip\"]\n          - [\"008a s0\", \"105K\", 3.1, 778, \"recovering\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Actor entropy vs step 多配置叠加图，collapsed 和 late-stage healthy 有 overlap region\"\n    analysis: >\n      Actor entropy 作为 standalone diagnostic 不具备足够 separating power。可作为\n      nve 的 supplementary metric，但不增加独立的 diagnostic 价值。对论文贡献边际。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: \"Distribution plots of V(s) vs Monte Carlo return\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_35K_value_mean: 60.2\n      walker_008d_35K_mc_return_mean: 146\n      walker_008d_35K_value_spread: \"bimodal: cluster near 0 + long right tail to 200\"\n      walker_008d_45K_value_shift: \"right tail extends to 350, MC returns peaked at 141\"\n      walker_baseline_35K_overlap: \"high — values well-calibrated, V(s) ≈ 0.8-1.2x MC\"\n      walker_008a_35K_overlap: \"moderate — V(s) slightly below MC (0.6-0.9x)\"\n      cross_env_consistency: \"Cheetah shows minimal V(s) divergence even for trained dt_emb\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 value distribution 分析在 Walker 中展示预期的 trained dt_emb 偏差——\n      008d 的 V(s) 分布出现右偏 heavy tail，高估部分 state 的 value。但问题在于：\n      (1) @35K 时这种 right tail 可能仍在 \"正常探索\" 范围内，和 baseline 的 V(s)\n      分布 overlap 显著；(2) 只有到 45K+ 才能清晰看到 divergence，此时 nve 已经\n      标记了问题——value distribution 分析没有提供比 nve 更早的 warning；(3) 在\n      Cheetah 中，trained dt_emb 的 V(s) 分布与 baseline 高度重叠（因为 nve 仅\n      1.1-1.3x），使得这个分析在 cross-env 上不一致。worst 档下这个分析是 \"confirms\n      nve findings with more detail but no additional predictive power\"。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"V(s) vs MC return scatter plot at 35K/45K/55K for 008d vs baseline\"\n      - \"V(s) distribution histogram overlay: 008d right-skewed vs baseline symmetric\"\n    analysis: >\n      Value distribution 分析提供了更 fine-grained 的 overestimation 可视化，但不增加\n      nve 以外的 diagnostic 能力。对论文价值在于 \"illustration\" 而非 \"new finding\"。\n      可纳入 appendix 而非 main paper。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: \"Cosine similarity between dt=1 and dt=2 learned embeddings\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_cosine_5K: 0.92\n      walker_008d_cosine_35K: 0.88\n      walker_008d_cosine_55K: 0.85\n      walker_006_cosine_35K: 0.87\n      cosine_evolution_trend: \"slow decrease (0.92→0.85) — embeddings only weakly differentiated\"\n      cheetah_trained_cosine_35K: 0.91\n      cross_env_cosine_difference: \"minimal\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 cosine similarity 分析揭示一个反直觉结果：dt=1 和 dt=2 的 learned\n      embedding 高度相似（cosine 0.85-0.92），且 evolution 缓慢。这与 \"trained dt_emb\n      enables precise dt prediction in imagination\" 的叙事矛盾——如果 embedding 这么\n      相似，critic 如何利用它们区分 dt？可能的解释是 embedding 空间中的微小差异\n      （cosine 0.85 意味着 ~30° 角度差）足以让 MLP critic head 区分，但这削弱了\n      \"dt_embedding 是 smoking gun\" 的叙事力度——embedding 差异如此微小，可能只是\n      整个 RSSM 表征的一个次要信号，而非 primary driver。在 Cheetah 中 cosine\n      相似度与 Walker 几乎相同（0.91 vs 0.88），但 Cheetah 没有 collapse——进一步\n      说明 cosine similarity 不是 predictive 的。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"dt Embedding Cosine Similarity Evolution\"\n        columns: [\"environment\", \"config\", \"step\", \"cos(dt=1, dt=2)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker\", \"008d\", \"5K\", 0.92]\n          - [\"Walker\", \"008d\", \"35K\", 0.88]\n          - [\"Walker\", \"008d\", \"55K (collapse)\", 0.85]\n          - [\"Walker\", \"006\", \"35K\", 0.87]\n          - [\"Cheetah\", \"trained\", \"35K\", 0.91]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cosine similarity vs training step，Walker 和 Cheetah 叠加，差异极小\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cosine similarity 分析结果 inconclusive。embedding 差异微小且 cross-env 一致，\n      但 outcome 不同——说明 embedding 本身不是 causal bottleneck，RSSM fidelity 才是。\n      可放入 appendix 作为 \"embedding analysis does not explain cross-env differences\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_050\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in non-locomotion DMC environment\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 820\n      seed1_eval_105K: 795\n      seed2_eval_105K: 840\n      IQM_3seeds: 818\n      seed0_ve_35K: 0.22\n      seed0_ve_105K: 0.62\n      ve_stable_range: \"60-65% from 125K+\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cartpole Swingup 是非 locomotion 环境，DreamerV3 baseline 应正常收敛。eval\n      在不同环境量级不同，Cartpole 可能在 800+ 范围收敛。v/e 校准与 Walker 和 Cheetah\n      又有不同（ve@35K ~0.22），为 cross-env 阈值统一增加第三个校准点的差异。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole Baseline\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"ve@35K\", \"ve@105K\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"seed 0\", 820, 0.22, 0.62]\n          - [\"seed 1\", 795, 0.20, 0.59]\n          - [\"seed 2\", 840, 0.24, 0.64]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole baseline 学习曲线\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline 正常。v/e 校准位于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_051\"\n    description: \"Replicate delusional critic collapse in Cartpole Swingup\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 480\n      seed0_nve_peak: 1.20\n      seed0_nve_105K: 0.88\n      seed0_collapse: false\n      seed1_eval_105K: 510\n      seed1_nve_peak: 1.15\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed2_eval_105K: 460\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.28\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      IQM_3seeds_105K: 483\n      IQM_pct_baseline: \"59%\"\n      nve_above_1_5x_count: \"0/3\"\n      collapse_count: \"0/3\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 Cheetah 相似的 non-replication。Cartpole Swingup 的 dynamics 虽然与 locomotion\n      不同（需要 swing + balance），但 RSSM 对 dt=2 步的预测误差仍然不够大到触发\n      delusional critic。obs_gap 预计约 1.45x（介于 Cheetah 的 1.35x 和 Walker 的 2.04x\n      之间），nve peak 约 1.15-1.28x，不达 1.5x 阈值。这是 worst 档最关键的证据——\n      两个独立的非 Walker 环境都不复现 nve>1.5x，证明 Walker 的 RSSM fidelity gap\n      是异常高的特例。cross_env_mechanism_replication 依然为 0。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole Trained dt_emb Results\"\n        columns: [\"seed\", \"eval@105K\", \"% baseline\", \"nve peak\", \"collapse\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"seed 0\", 480, \"59%\", \"1.20x\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"seed 1\", 510, \"62%\", \"1.15x\", \"NO\"]\n          - [\"seed 2\", 460, \"56%\", \"1.28x\", \"NO\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole nve 轨迹三 seed，全部低于 1.5x 阈值线\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cartpole 的 non-replication 与 Cheetah 形成合力，确认 \"nve>1.5x diagnostic\"\n      是 Walker-specific。C2 的 generalizability 为零。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_052\"\n    description: \"Replicate causal control in Cartpole Swingup\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 465\n      seed0_nve_105K: 0.82\n      seed1_eval_105K: 490\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.90\n      seed2_eval_105K: 445\n      seed2_nve_105K: 0.85\n      IQM_3seeds_105K: 467\n      IQM_pct_baseline: \"57%\"\n      trained_vs_untrained_eval_gap: \"~3% (483 vs 467)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 Cheetah 相同的模式：trained vs untrained dt_emb 的差异极小（3%），因为 Cartpole\n      的 RSSM fidelity gap 不足以使 dt_emb 产生有意义的因果效应。degradation 主要\n      来自 subsample ON 的学习信号减少。两组的 nve 分布高度重叠（trained 0.88-1.28x\n      vs untrained 0.82-0.90x），不具 separating power。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole: Trained vs No dt_emb\"\n        columns: [\"config\", \"IQM eval@105K\", \"IQM nve@105K\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"trained dt_emb (051)\", 483, \"1.07x\"]\n          - [\"no dt_emb (052)\", 467, \"0.86x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole 两配置 nve violin plot，严重 overlap\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cartpole 确认 Cheetah 的发现：dt_emb 在低 RSSM-fidelity-gap 环境中无因果效应。\n\n  - name: \"Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_060\"\n    description: \"Pilot feasibility of RSSM-uncertainty-based imagination truncation\"\n    expected_results:\n      eval_return_35K: 180\n      eval_return_45K: 210\n      eval_return_55K: 195\n      eval_return_65K: 170\n      eval_return_105K: 250\n      vs_baseline_105K: \"-73%\"\n      avg_imagination_length: 4.2\n      truncation_frequency: \"62% of rollouts truncated before H=15\"\n      nve_105K: 0.95\n      uncertainty_calibration: \"poor — std overestimates in early training, underestimates in late\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 uncertainty-gated truncation 的核心问题是 RSSM 的 uncertainty 估计\n      不可靠。DreamerV3 的 RSSM 使用 categorical latent（不是 Gaussian），其\n      uncertainty 没有 principled calibration。pilot 实现可能使用 ensemble disagreement\n      或 reconstruction error 作为 proxy，但这些 proxy 在 worst 档下表现不佳：\n      (1) 早期训练时 uncertainty 全面偏高，导致 rollout 过早截断（avg 仅 4.2 步，\n      vs H=15），学习信号极度不足；(2) 晚期训练时 RSSM 变得 overconfident，uncertainty\n      偏低，不再截断 — 但此时可能 dt=2 预测已经出现偏差。结果是 performance 仅\n      250@105K (27% baseline)，比 008d collapse (83@55K) 好但比 008a (778) 和 008e_v3\n      (870) 差很多。truncation 阈值难以 tune — 太紧学不了，太松不防崩。这使得\n      uncertainty-gated 方法在当前 RSSM 架构下不 feasible，削弱了 \"future work\"\n      方向的可信度。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Truncation Pilot Results\"\n        columns: [\"metric\", \"value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"eval@105K\", 250]\n          - [\"% baseline\", \"27%\"]\n          - [\"avg imagination length\", \"4.2 / 15 steps\"]\n          - [\"truncation rate\", \"62%\"]\n          - [\"nve@105K\", \"0.95x\"]\n          - [\"collapse\", \"NO\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Imagination length histogram at 35K vs 75K vs 105K，显示 truncation 行为随训练变化\"\n      - \"Uncertainty calibration plot: predicted uncertainty vs actual prediction error\"\n    analysis: >\n      Uncertainty-gated truncation 在 pilot 中不 feasible，主要因 RSSM uncertainty\n      calibration 差。不能作为 \"practical future direction\" 推荐，只能作为 \"open\n      challenge\" 讨论。论文的 actionable takeaway 进一步缩窄到 \"use dt=1 imagination\"\n      这一简单但 limited 的建议。\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: \"Third DMC locomotion environment for generalization\"\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_IQM: 250\n      trained_dt_emb_IQM: 145\n      trained_dt_emb_pct_baseline: \"58%\"\n      trained_dt_emb_nve_peak_range: \"[1.10, 1.35]\"\n      trained_dt_emb_collapse_count: \"0/3\"\n      no_dt_emb_IQM: 138\n      no_dt_emb_pct_baseline: \"55%\"\n      trained_vs_untrained_gap: \"~5%\"\n      cross_env_replication: 0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Hopper Hop 作为第三个 locomotion 环境，在 worst 档下与 Cheetah 表现一致——\n      trained dt_emb 不触发 nve>1.5x，无 collapse。Hopper 的 dynamics 虽然比 Cheetah\n      更非线性（hopping requires contact dynamics），但 RSSM 的 dt=2 预测误差仍不足\n      以触发正反馈 loop（预计 obs_gap ~1.55x，低于 Walker 的 2.04x）。degradation\n      pattern 是 uniform 的 plateau（~58% baseline），trained vs untrained dt_emb 差异\n      仅 ~5%。三个非 Walker 环境（Cheetah, Cartpole, Hopper）统一不复现，确认\n      Walker 的 delusional critic 是 environment-specific outlier。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Hopper Hop Summary\"\n        columns: [\"config\", \"IQM eval@105K\", \"% baseline\", \"nve peak\", \"collapse\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"baseline\", 250, \"100%\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", 145, \"58%\", \"1.25x\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"no dt_emb\", 138, \"55%\", \"0.90x\", \"0/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Hopper 三配置 bar chart with error bars\"\n    analysis: >\n      Hopper 进一步巩固 non-replication 结论。四个环境中仅 Walker 展示 delusional critic。\n\n  # ---- Cross-cutting summary metrics for worst tier ----\n\n  - name: \"Worst Tier Aggregate Assessment\"\n    plan_id: \"aggregate\"\n    description: \"Cross-experiment summary metrics defining the worst tier\"\n    expected_results:\n      C6_recovery_pct_of_baseline: 73\n      nve_threshold_classification_accuracy: 0.67\n      cross_env_mechanism_replication: 0\n      collapse_prob_trained_dt_emb: 0.11\n      walker_008e_v3_IQM_pct_baseline: 73\n      walker_nve_separating_power: 0.67\n      total_collapse_events: \"1/9 (Walker 008d s0 only)\"\n      environments_with_nve_above_1_5x: \"1/4 (Walker only, 2/3 seeds)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      跨所有实验的聚合视图。collapse 概率 1/9 = 11%（9 个 trained dt_emb seed 中仅 1 个\n      collapse：Walker 008d seed 0）。nve>1.5x 仅在 Walker 中出现（2/3 seeds），其他\n      三个环境（Cheetah 0/3, Cartpole 0/3, Hopper 0/3）无一超过。1.5x 阈值在 Walker\n      内部的 classification accuracy 为 4/6 = 67%（trained 2/3 exceed + untrained\n      008f s1 1/3 也 exceed）。C6 mitigation 的 cross-seed IQM 仅 73%。\n      这些数字共同指向一个结论：原来的 \"universal diagnostic mechanism\" 叙事不成立，\n      论文必须 reframe 为 \"Walker-specific case study + diagnostic methodology contribution\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-Environment Mechanism Summary\"\n        columns: [\"environment\", \"trained dt_emb nve>1.5x\", \"collapse\", \"untrained nve>1.5x\", \"dt_emb causal effect\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"2/3 (67%)\", \"1/3 (33%)\", \"1/3 (33%)\", \"moderate\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"negligible\"]\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"negligible\"]\n          - [\"Hopper Hop\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"0/3 (0%)\", \"negligible\"]\n          - [\"TOTAL\", \"2/12 (17%)\", \"1/12 (8%)\", \"1/12 (8%)\", \"—\"]\n      - name: \"Paper Claim Viability Under Worst Tier\"\n        columns: [\"claim\", \"original strength\", \"worst tier strength\", \"reframe needed\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"C1 (degradation)\", \"Strong\", \"Strong\", \"NO — all configs degrade everywhere\"]\n          - [\"C2 (nve>1.5x diagnostic)\", \"Moderate-strong\", \"Weak\", \"YES — Walker-only, classification 67%\"]\n          - [\"C3 (value suppression)\", \"Strong\", \"Moderate\", \"YES — direction holds, magnitude varies\"]\n          - [\"C4 (dt amplification)\", \"Moderate\", \"Moderate\", \"NO — still only 2 dt values\"]\n          - [\"C5 (horizon/subsample)\", \"Moderate\", \"Moderate-strong\", \"YES — becomes PRIMARY factor in Cheetah\"]\n          - [\"C6 (mitigation)\", \"Moderate-strong\", \"Weak-moderate\", \"YES — 73% IQM, high variance\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Hero figure: 4-environment × 3-config heatmap of nve peak, with 1.5x threshold contour showing Walker isolation\"\n      - \"Forest plot: C6 mitigation % baseline across seeds and environments with CI\"\n    analysis: >\n      Worst 档下论文的可行叙事：(1) C1 保持不变（degradation is universal）；(2) C2 降级\n      为 Walker case study，但 reframe 为 \"failure mode is architecture×environment\n      interaction\"；(3) C5 升级为 Cheetah/Cartpole/Hopper 的 primary explanatory\n      factor（learning signal reduction, not delusional critic）；(4) RSSM fidelity table\n      作为核心方法论贡献，解释 why failure modes differ across environments；\n      (5) C6 降级为 environment-conditional guideline。标题改为问句形式：\n      \"When Does Temporal Abstraction Break World Models?\"——承认答案是 conditional。\n      CoRL 预期 borderline：methodology novelty（factorial ablation + nve protocol）\n      可能获得一个审稿人的认可，但 lack of generalizable findings 会被另一个审稿人\n      视为 insufficient contribution。补充 plan_032 的 value distribution 分析可增加\n      分析深度但不改变核心问题。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d0c2338d-48fd-4569-bbff-a85af5e5ab47","total_cost_usd":0.822676,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30708,"cache_read_input_tokens":54082,"output_tokens":23129,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30708,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":22993,"cache_read_input_tokens":42241,"cache_creation_input_tokens":308,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":308},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":25360,"outputTokens":22,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.02547,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":3,"outputTokens":23129,"cacheReadInputTokens":54082,"cacheCreationInputTokens":30708,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.797206,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"48917d87-a105-43cc-8c06-998b1c9fd3b8"}
